d36898ea0a7f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7666455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/artokun","id":7666455,"login":"artokun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NjY0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commits/c19871f0d995a30a499c30be0831cf50c20ffe3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:27:02Z","email":"art.longbottom.jr@gmail.com","name":"Arthur R Longbottom"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:27:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(2201): preserve panel-wide chat when canonical history is unavailable (#2214)\n\n* fix(2201): preserve panel-wide chat when canonical history is unavailable\n\nDo not treat an IndexedDB open timeout or other canonical-read miss as an empty archive during a workflow remount. Keep the tab thread/session pointers and retry hydration until a positively available snapshot can bind or confirm a reset.\n\n* fix(2201): decide canonical availability by the TRANSACTION, and never apply a stale hydration\n\nTwo review findings, both real, both with a destructive edge.\n\n1. `idbRead` resolved in `req.onsuccess`. A `get` can succeed and its transaction\n   abort afterwards — and because the promise was already settled, the\n   `tx.onerror`/`tx.onabort` handlers were DEAD CODE. An aborted read therefore\n   reported `available: true`, and `load()` promoted a possibly-trimmed\n   localStorage shadow as the write intent: exactly the reset this issue is about.\n   Availability now comes from `tx.oncomplete`.\n\n2. The hydration retry was cancelled only by `destroy()`, so it could not see a\n   user who selected or created a chat while IndexedDB was recovering. Applying\n   then reselected the MOUNT-time thread, repainted its transcript over the one\n   they were reading, and could fence an in-flight reply. It now re-validates the\n   thread pointer before applying, and binds from the LIVE session pointer so a\n   session rotated while waiting is not reverted to the mount-time capture.\n\nFOUR TEST DOUBLES had to be corrected first, and they were wrong in two different\nways — which is why (1) could ship at all:\n\n- three fired `tx.oncomplete` only for WRITES, so any reader that correctly waits\n  for the transaction hung forever rather than failing;\n- `legacy-shadow-quota` settled a READONLY transaction synchronously at creation,\n  i.e. before its own get handler ran — backwards from real IDB, where complete\n  fires after the request handlers.\n\nA fake that cannot model transaction completion cannot test code that depends on\nit; that file''s own header already says the same thing about keys.\n\nFull panel gate: 8263 unit tests (8262 pass, 1 todo), check-panel-scope OK (it\ncould not run in this worktree until node_modules was linked — and it is the only\ngate that catches a name resolving in a sibling function, which is exactly the\nshape of the guard added here), typecheck and check-tool-vocabulary clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n* fix(2201): drop the plan.retry flag nobody read\n\nSELF-REVIEW (codex out of tokens until 2026-09-06).\n\n`planRemountHistoryRestore` returned `{ kind: \"preserve\", retry: true }`. Nothing\nreads `retry`: the caller branches on `kind === \"preserve\"` and starts the retry\nfrom that. A second field asserting what `kind` already says was carried to no\none, and two encodings of the same fact are how the two drift apart.\n\nWorth recording HOW it survived. I ran a mechanical sweep over every field added\nacross these PRs specifically to catch this, and it passed `retry` — the regex was\nline-anchored (`^+  foo:`) and this is an INLINE property inside a one-line object\nliteral, which is exactly where short flags live. Found by reading the consumer\ninstead.\n\nThe procedure is now written to extract both shapes; the sweep is only worth\nhaving if it cannot quietly agree with me.\n\nFull panel gate: 8273 unit tests (8272 pass, 1 todo), check-panel-scope OK.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"949fa345eefe7b9200acd86344d179b8c4a885cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/git/trees/949fa345eefe7b9200acd86344d179b8c4a885cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/git/commits/c19871f0d995a30a499c30be0831cf50c20ffe3f","verification":{"payload":"tree 949fa345eefe7b9200acd86344d179b8c4a885cf\nparent 193931209aa6f495b84fbee9ab7e4f458444676d\nauthor Arthur R Longbottom <art.longbottom.jr@gmail.com> 1788510422 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788510422 -0700\n\nfix(2201): preserve panel-wide chat when canonical history is unavailable (#2214)\n\n* fix(2201): preserve panel-wide chat when canonical history is unavailable\n\nDo not treat an IndexedDB open timeout or other canonical-read miss as an empty archive during a workflow remount. Keep the tab thread/session pointers and retry hydration until a positively available snapshot can bind or confirm a reset.\n\n* fix(2201): decide canonical availability by the TRANSACTION, and never apply a stale hydration\n\nTwo review findings, both real, both with a destructive edge.\n\n1. `idbRead` resolved in `req.onsuccess`. A `get` can succeed and its transaction\n   abort afterwards — and because the promise was already settled, the\n   `tx.onerror`/`tx.onabort` handlers were DEAD CODE. An aborted read therefore\n   reported `available: true`, and `load()` promoted a possibly-trimmed\n   localStorage shadow as the write intent: exactly the reset this issue is about.\n   Availability now comes from `tx.oncomplete`.\n\n2. The hydration retry was cancelled only by `destroy()`, so it could not see a\n   user who selected or created a chat while IndexedDB was recovering. Applying\n   then reselected the MOUNT-time thread, repainted its transcript over the one\n   they were reading, and could fence an in-flight reply. It now re-validates the\n   thread pointer before applying, and binds from the LIVE session pointer so a\n   session rotated while waiting is not reverted to the mount-time capture.\n\nFOUR TEST DOUBLES had to be corrected first, and they were wrong in two different\nways — which is why (1) could ship at all:\n\n- three fired `tx.oncomplete` only for WRITES, so any reader that correctly waits\n  for the transaction hung forever rather than failing;\n- `legacy-shadow-quota` settled a READONLY transaction synchronously at creation,\n  i.e. before its own get handler ran — backwards from real IDB, where complete\n  fires after the request handlers.\n\nA fake that cannot model transaction completion cannot test code that depends on\nit; that file''s own header already says the same thing about keys.\n\nFull panel gate: 8263 unit tests (8262 pass, 1 todo), check-panel-scope OK (it\ncould not run in this worktree until node_modules was linked — and it is the only\ngate that catches a name resolving in a sibling function, which is exactly the\nshape of the guard added here), typecheck and check-tool-vocabulary clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n* fix(2201): drop the plan.retry flag nobody read\n\nSELF-REVIEW (codex out of tokens until 2026-09-06).\n\n`planRemountHistoryRestore` returned `{ kind: \"preserve\", retry: true }`. Nothing\nreads `retry`: the caller branches on `kind === \"preserve\"` and starts the retry\nfrom that. A second field asserting what `kind` already says was carried to no\none, and two encodings of the same fact are how the two drift apart.\n\nWorth recording HOW it survived. I ran a mechanical sweep over every field added\nacross these PRs specifically to catch this, and it passed `retry` — the regex was\nline-anchored (`^+  foo:`) and this is an INLINE property inside a one-line object\nliteral, which is exactly where short flags live. Found by reading the consumer\ninstead.\n\nThe procedure is now written to extract both shapes; the sweep is only worth\nhaving if it cannot quietly agree with me.\n\nFull panel gate: 8273 unit tests (8272 pass, 1 todo), check-panel-scope OK.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmoDWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArfoQAAwtb8wUwI6nxUoav1GF6UmX\nh0mrWTqS35qrGfx/YB+SZOI7fXVYyf3NniFbcvtkV9HKqT5b9j2kWPigQIbD4M7f\nnY82Ym0o/zsauHUs44UfnzYb6kyqBR2W1NzIHzQX6yobxAjqD2sx3ouNtpwy91rT\nojDryfbD2IHeRottXwWiR6S4AwmbLavshobbvgKI7XPcMzq3TyZwRHitNkzIOyET\nDPRM/alkssOkOL1IPRSlsf3wr30c2ARoouF91kty7OX2rfDS9Dl1UVgCxco5GtUt\nTYXVTrsM6xXlL8u2SJavJ0/+dmF/0AzN8KheR/s79PTc5MYLEuM61RZ8lpJ/6hsJ\n52sRr28HP/EfxKlR1qxRpggGuGIDUs+vxo3TXIKtl+6eGBRFttiW1hgm1zB2P+dA\ntheI5o3blw5GN0ME6PZ46IpBksaZgJQ16+8XLarkIb