url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/artokun","id":7666455,"login":"artokun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NjY0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commits/d9cdda1ce00a9c5a58d05b7c3cf339a87c1193dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:22:54Z","email":"art.longbottom.jr@gmail.com","name":"Artokun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:22:54Z","email":"art.longbottom.jr@gmail.com","name":"Artokun"},"message":"chore: merge main and re-file the Unreleased entry\n\nA merge landed on main (#2236), conflicting every open branch on CHANGELOG.md.\nReset to main''s file and INSERTED this branch''s own entries into main''s Unreleased\nsection rather than replacing it: unlike a release, a merge leaves other PRs''\nentries sitting in that block, and replacing the body deletes them. Verified both\ndirections — this branch''s entries present, and main''s still there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y","tree":{"sha":"c175b8ed2509d1ae329d5fea8e687904e82c5e0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/git/trees/c175b8ed2509d1ae329d5fea8e687904e82c5e0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/git/commits/d9cdda1ce00a9c5a58d05b7c3cf339a87c1193dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7666455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/artokun","id":7666455,"login":"artokun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NjY0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commit/d9cdda1ce00a9c5a58d05b7c3cf339a87c1193dc","node_id":"C_kwDOS48I39oAKGQ5Y2RkYTFjZTAwYTljNWE1OGQwNWI3YzNjZjMzOWE4N2MxMTkzZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commit/c62fe1ccc05720f7db78303bc49c25ad1f0d4bd8","sha":"c62fe1ccc05720f7db78303bc49c25ad1f0d4bd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commits/c62fe1ccc05720f7db78303bc49c25ad1f0d4bd8"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commit/193931209aa6f495b84fbee9ab7e4f458444676d","sha":"193931209aa6f495b84fbee9ab7e4f458444676d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commits/193931209aa6f495b84fbee9ab7e4f458444676d"}],"sha":"d9cdda1ce00a9c5a58d05b7c3cf339a87c1193dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commits/d9cdda1ce00a9c5a58d05b7c3cf339a87c1193dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7666455?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/artokun","id":7666455,"login":"artokun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NjY0NTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/artokun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/commits/193931209aa6f495b84fbee9ab7e4f458444676d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:12:03Z","email":"art.longbottom.jr@gmail.com","name":"Arthur R Longbottom"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:12:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(2203): recover prompt_id when panel_run fetch fails after dispatch (#2215)\n\n* fix(2203): recover prompt_id when panel_run fetch fails after dispatch\n\nStamp a client dispatch id onto extra_data before POST /prompt, then reconcile it against /queue and /history if the fetch throws or returns no receipt. A unique match restores the prompt_id; a confirmed miss is safe to retry.\n\n* test(2203): drive the post-dispatch recovery poll with no real timer\n\nCI failed with a cluster of `cancelledByParent` on run-scope-guard.test.mjs:\n\n    error: ''Promise resolution is still pending but the event loop has\n            already resolved''\n\nThe first casualty was the #556 r6 \"fetch THROWS\" case; everything after it in\nthe file was cancelled, which made a dozen unrelated tests look broken.\n\nCause: the #2203 recovery polls /queue then /history up to four times and\nsleeps 40ms between attempts with a REAL setTimeout. Neither call site in\nrun-scope-guard forwarded the pacing, so unit tests always paid ~120ms of\nwall-clock per recovery. When the runner drains the event loop before those\ntimers fire -- a loaded CI runner, not this machine -- node reports the pending\npromise and cancels the file. It passes locally either way, which is why it\nlooked like a product failure rather than a timer.\n\n`recoverPromptIdAfterDispatch` was already designed to be driven (`delayMs`,\n`sleep`); the guard just never threaded it. Now both factories accept an\noptional `recoverDelayMs`, defaulting to today''s behaviour, and the tests pass\n0 -- at which point the poll skips the sleep entirely (`i > 0 && wait > 0`) and\nschedules no timer at all.\n\nDeterministic rather than a widened tolerance, and the adjacent test''s existing\n`keepAlive()` band-aid is no longer the only defence.\n\nMeasured: run-scope-guard.test.mjs 4412ms -> 3651ms, so the timers really are\ngone. Full unit suite 8254 passed, 0 failed, 0 cancelled; typecheck and\ncheck-tool-vocabulary clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n* wip\n\n* fix(2203): address review — stop the recovery claiming more than it observed\n\nFour review findings, all real. Three of them are the same failure: the module\nauthorizing a retry, or a receipt, on evidence that cannot support it.\n\n1. A unique QUEUE MARK was returned as `recovered`. It is not a per-dispatch\n   receipt: every prompt in a batch shares it, and the counter restarts on page\n   reload while ComfyUI history persists. A single match can therefore name an\n   earlier batch item or a previous session''s row — reporting a stale prompt_id\n   AND counting this failed post as observed. It is now reported as `markMatch`\n   for the human and the VERDICT stays unknown.\n\n2. `readJson` parsed non-2xx bodies. A 500 `/history` answering `{error: ...}`\n   read as a valid, empty history map; with an empty queue that became `absent`\n   and authorized a retry on the strength of the server being broken. Only 2xx\n   counts now.\n\n3. The confirmed-miss message promised the request \"is safe to retry\". A bounded\n   sequence of empty reads cannot prove a request will not be accepted AFTER the\n   last one. It now names the miss, says the observation is bounded, and tells the\n   caller to check the queue when a duplicate would be expensive. The test whose\n   NAME encoded the old contract was renamed with it.\n\n4. `missingPromptIds` was banked by `onMissingPromptId` BEFORE recovery ran and\n   never taken back, so a receipt successfully recovered from the queue still\n   carried uncertainCount > 0 and reported `queued_unknown` instead of accepted.\n   The unscoped branch already ordered this correctly; the scoped one did not.\n\n(4) was UNPINNED — reverting it broke nothing — so it has its own test now, and\nthat test fails when the increment moves back ahead of recovery.\n\nFull panel gate: 8277 unit tests (8276 pass, 1 todo), typecheck and\ncheck-tool-vocabulary clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n* fix(2203): drop the markMatch field nobody read\n\nSELF-REVIEW of my own change from earlier today (codex out of tokens until\n2026-09-06).\n\nWhen the queue-mark match was downgraded from `recovered` to `unknown` — correct,\nsince the mark is shared across a batch and its counter restarts on reload — I\nattached the matched prompt_id as `markMatch`, with a comment saying it was\n\"still worth reporting as corroboration\".\n\nNothing reported it. Both callers of `recoverPromptIdAfterDispatch` do\n\n    if (recovered.status !== \"recovered\") return false;\n\nand drop everything else, so the field reached no one and the comment claiming\notherwise was false. Its only reader was the test asserting it exists.\n\nThat is the same defect I have spent the day finding in other people''s code and\nmy own: a producer carrying something the consumer discards. Carrying it \"in case\nsomeone wants it later\" is the rationalisation that leaves dead data around, so it\nis gone. If a human ever needs the corroborating id in the failure message, it\nshould arrive together with the consumer that shows it.\n\nFull panel gate: 8287 unit tests (8286 pass, 1 todo), check-panel-scope OK.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f85459028a01fd5df82acb76d3d8f03f7de0eab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/git/trees/6f85459028a01fd5df82acb76d3d8f03f7de0eab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/artokun/comfyui-mcp-panel/git/commits/193931209aa6f495b84fbee9ab7e4f458444676d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f85459028a01fd5df82acb76d3d8f03f7de0eab\nparent f66cfc0c731f50b906cf43ba723bf53a710277a4\nauthor Arthur R Longbottom <art.longbottom.jr@gmail.com> 1788509523 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788509523 -0700\n\nfix(2203): recover prompt_id when panel_run fetch fails after dispatch (#2215)\n\n* fix(2203): recover prompt_id when panel_run fetch fails after dispatch\n\nStamp a client dispatch id onto extra_data before POST /prompt, then reconcile it against /queue and /history if the fetch throws or returns no receipt. A unique match restores the prompt_id; a confirmed miss is safe to retry.\n\n* test(2203): drive the post-dispatch recovery poll with no real timer\n\nCI failed with a cluster of `cancelledByParent` on run-scope-guard.test.mjs:\n\n    error: ''Promise resolution is still pending but the event loop has\n            already resolved''\n\nThe first casualty was the #556 r6 \"fetch THROWS\" case; everything after it in\nthe file was cancelled, which made a dozen unrelated tests look broken.\n\nCause: the #2203 recovery polls /queue then /history up to four times and\nsleeps 40ms between attempts with a REAL setTimeout. Neither call site in\nrun-scope-guard forwarded the pacing, so unit tests always paid ~120ms of\nwall-clock per recovery. When the runner drains the event loop before those\ntimers fire -- a loaded CI runner, not this machine -- node reports the pending\npromise and cancels the file. It passes locally either way, which is why it\nlooked like a product failure rather than a timer.\n\n`recoverPromptIdAfterDispatch` was already designed to be driven (`delayMs`,\n`sleep`); the guard just never threaded it. Now both factories accept an\noptional `recoverDelayMs`, defaulting to today''s behaviour, and the tests pass\n0 -- at which point the poll skips the sleep entirely (`i > 0 && wait > 0`) and\nschedules no timer at all.\n\nDeterministic rather than a widened tolerance, and the adjacent test''s existing\n`keepAlive()` band-aid is no longer the only defence.\n\nMeasured: run-scope-guard.test.mjs 4412ms -> 3651ms, so the timers really are\ngone. Full unit suite 8254 passed, 0 failed, 0 cancelled; typecheck and\ncheck-tool-vocabulary clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n* wip\n\n* fix(2203): address review — stop the recovery claiming more than it observed\n\nFour review findings, all real. Three of them are the same failure: the module\nauthorizing a retry, or a receipt, on evidence that cannot support it.\n\n1. A unique QUEUE MARK was returned as `recovered`. It is not a per-dispatch\n   receipt: every prompt in a batch shares it, and the counter restarts on page\n   reload while ComfyUI history persists. A single match can therefore name an\n   earlier batch item or a previous session''s row — reporting a stale prompt_id\n   AND counting this failed post as observed. It is now reported as `markMatch`\n   for the human and the VERDICT stays unknown.\n\n2. `readJson` parsed non-2xx bodies. A 500 `/history` answering `{error: ...}`\n   read as a valid, empty history map; with an empty queue that became `absent`\n   and authorized a retry on the strength of the server being broken. Only 2xx\n   counts now.\n\n3. The confirmed-miss message promised the request \"is safe to retry\". A bounded\n   sequence of empty reads cannot prove a request will not be accepted AFTER the\n   last one. It now names the miss, says the observation is bounded, and tells the\n   caller to check the queue when a duplicate would be expensive. The test whose\n   NAME encoded the old contract was renamed with it.\n\n4. `missingPromptIds` was banked by `onMissingPromptId` BEFORE recovery ran and\n   never taken back, so a receipt successfully recovered from the queue still\n   carried uncertainCount > 0 and reported `queued_unknown` instead of accepted.\n   The unscoped branch already ordered this correctly; the scoped one did not.\n\n(4) was UNPINNED — reverting it broke nothing — so it has its own test now, and\nthat test fails when the increment moves back ahead of recovery.\n\nFull panel gate: 8277 unit tests (8276 pass, 1 todo), typecheck and\ncheck-tool-vocabulary clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n* fix(2203): drop the markMatch field nobody read\n\nSELF-REVIEW of my own change from earlier today (codex out of tokens until\n2026-09-06).\n\nWhen the queue-mark match was downgraded from `recovered` to `unknown` — correct,\nsince the mark is shared across a batch and its counter restarts on reload — I\nattached the matched prompt_id as `markMatch`, with a comment saying it was\n\"still worth reporting as corroboration\".\n\nNothing reported it. Both callers of `recoverPromptIdAfterDispatch` do\n\n    if (recovered.status !== \"recovered\") return false;\n\nand drop everything else, so the field reached no one and the comment claiming\notherwise was false. Its only reader was the test asserting it exists.\n\nThat is the same defect I have spent the day finding in other people''s code and\nmy own: a producer carrying something the consumer discards. Carrying it \"in case\nsomeone wants it later\" is the rationalisation that leaves dead data around, so it\nis gone. If a human ever needs the corroborating id in the failure message, it\nshould arrive together with the consumer that shows it.\n\nFull panel gate: 8287 unit tests (8286 pass, 1 todo), check-panel-scope OK.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GqXS5Qys1hiK9aDdXJRJ6Y\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmn1TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm8sQAFCPLOgttdbupy9JeDsswbOp\nXg7NFqehva+4uofWCQNTkdeCrqx//2umj4m3t6C3X1qDWyxuF5GSsEnZjBXUe7V7\nHmPaLAb1bkWVA2PppRApqly1ICoOv/8HQptdCFJrY9Gi8cUSCpUg0K+ozDmAGxD6\ncoN+QHBW0meM8Fw/GDBYe//aIScrvX8x8ugWS5R6P575x3oY0NcHA8ttwwZQW+Pk\nJW4BOskYBC0MWZHLL8Ha+D4P7IUjYez95fMDwfDPZGwlFZU/OXY6jI/wwDIpJ3x2\ndvJHSY2atsUJTJpKb9UpXI6e2pXrOuftK+XdyQULGjSLw0Fr8WD8w4RMC2qdqm2h\n1iFFLw8qIGqD26nuqpb+fl4z5kEwtVT8f0lhkEv5oL1tOc+64lO9/OVuJIrZEaqT\nvMqSahg+4qwJKozQeCKu5WYQfEsc56vXyErk8Oaku1Zm4gHVASdYzbQHCjUI6usB\nDOP9wVzXrHtRuTEkXVtKQsHjdoMOmgwpkEFgmZxvOUEO60awkkk/D6wHFQ1xWgbA\nptbUGjCKeOQtjI5HzT0nAy3iIEPvYQjM9p51YeMXM92KR+/ORilPLMcXnUKbayvN\nu0z+z9ETp9ARdIPMj9ABGUjg37zaBNvS5jHspEP2AOACQIPTrL/sU2meJG1HJFke\nHjRIklKkFlHE1UyKWzrq\n=UcMH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T08:12:04Z"}},"committer