om/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-app-studio/commits/06794dde6cb61b05ca7a63bfdf90df954bf6f27b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:38:02Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:38:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Take the upstream fixes for four new govulncheck findings (#783)\n\n* Take the upstream fixes for four new govulncheck findings\n\nThe vulnerability database gained four entries the gate reaches from this\ntree, and each has a fix to take rather than an exposure to accept:\n\n  GO-2026-6497, GO-2026-6499  oras.land/oras-go/v2            2.6.1 -> 2.6.2\n  GO-2026-6505                otel otlptrace exporters         1.44  -> 1.45\n  GO-2026-6597                github.com/containerd/containerd 1.7.35 -> 1.7.36\n\nThe otel one needs the grpc and http exporter modules bumped as well as the\nparent: they are separate modules and the advisory names all three. Root and\nproviders/edges carry them; provider-sdk does not. Both gates pass locally.\n\n* Carry the same fixes into every module that links the affected packages\n\nThe vulnerability database is read live, and the first pass bumped only the\ntwo modules the gate had failed on by then. Every module that links the\notel trace exporters needs the same pin — provider-sdk directly, and\nquickstart through its provider-sdk replace, where otel itself had to follow\nto 1.45 for the exporters'' semconv. The modules that replace the root\nmodule (agents) only needed their go.sum brought up to date with the root''s\nnew graph; without that the agents image stopped building.\n\nEvery module builds and every govulncheck gate passes locally.","tree":{"sha":"c6045c7ee703f21b325f693f0d2882e7879aac9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-app-studio/git/trees/c6045c7ee703f21b325f693f0d2882e7879aac9a"},"url":"https://