rl":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/5e8ef12cc7ff5597b5d0c4eb85cf6aa7d03688cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:23:12Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:23:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Codex/semantic bi agent experience (#778)\n\n* fix(portalkit): preserve resource header action layout\n\n* feat(agents): add inline charts and durable conversation history","tree":{"sha":"cba0131946065b7bac85ea35cbffd9b89401e95e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/cba0131946065b7bac85ea35cbffd9b89401e95e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/5e8ef12cc7ff5597b5d0c4eb85cf6aa7d03688cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/5e8ef12cc7ff5597b5d0c4eb85cf6aa7d03688cc","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDVlOGVmMTJjYzdmZjU1OTdiNWQwYzRlYjg1Y2Y2YWE3ZDAzNjg4Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667","sha":"1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667"}],"sha":"5e8ef12cc7ff5597b5d0c4eb85cf6aa7d03688cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/5e8ef12cc7ff5597b5d0c4eb85cf6aa7d03688cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:37:11Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:37:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adjust providers machinery (#777)\n\n* Fix nerw provider struct\n\n* Adjust providers logic\n\n* Move to better providers machinery\n\n* move provider contract\n\n* fix CI\n\n* Claim the kind a required verb coordinate hangs off\n\nkcp refuses an APIExport whose permission claim names a custom\nsubresource without a claim on the resource that serves it. App Studio\nrequired code.railgrid.ai connections/mint-registry-token but never\nconnections, so `init` died at admission:\n\n  spec.permissionClaims[13].resource: Invalid value:\n  \"connections/mint-registry-token\": a claim on a custom subresource\n  requires a claim on \"connections\", which is what serves it\n\nApp Studio does read those Connections — it lists them when a project\npicks one and gets one back when a view resolves its connectionRef — so\nthe claim was simply missing, not deliberately absent. Declare it\nread-only and regenerate the export.\n\nValidateProviderRequirement now rejects a verb coordinate whose parent is\nnot declared in the same requirement, in either order, so the next one\nfails in `make verify` with the coordinate named rather than at a\nprovider''s own bootstrap.\n\nThe infrastructure provider e2e reported \"provider init failed: exit\nstatus 1\" and left the reason in a temp file CI does not upload; tail it\nto stderr.\n\nAgents ran with the WRONG identity: run-provider-agents resolved\nRAILGRID_PROVIDER_KUBECONFIG by taking the first file that existed out of\nthe provider''s own kubeconfig, kcp''s admin kubeconfig and the Tilt front\nproxy''s. Started before `agents-init` mints the first, it silently bound\nto kcp-admin, which authenticates but holds nothing in the provider\nworkspace, so every data-plane verb failed the gate:\n\n  dataplane: reading APIExportEndpointSlice agents.railgrid.ai:\n  Unauthorized\n\nserving HTTP 500 to the portal''s model discovery, and the controllers\nlogged Unauthorized lease errors on a loop. A verb runs as the provider,\nso no other identity will do: use the provider''s own kubeconfig or refuse\nto start, and watch the file in Tilt so init''s write restarts serve —\nwhat kuery and infrastructure already do.\n\n* Accept every requirement kuery declares when enabling it\n\nTestKueryAggregatesEdgeObjects failed with kuery unable to discover the\nedge''s Kubernetes API:\n\n  kuery engage: discovery failed for cluster 1vqly0gm36vbqs0b/kuery-k8s:\n  unknown\n\nThe edges provider never saw the request. kcp refused it first:\n\n  authorization step reason=\"failed to find suitable reason to allow\n  access in APIBinding\" decision=\"Denied\" resource=\"kubernetesclusters\"\n  subresource=\"k8s\" verb=\"get\" ... resp=403\n\nThe tenant''s APIBinding asked for three claims and accepted one. Its\nexportPermissionClaims carried kubernetesclusters, kubernetesclusters/k8s\nand subjectaccessreviews; appliedPermissionClaims carried only\nkubernetesclusters, because the test''s Enable ticked that one kind by\nname. A claim the binding does not accept is a coordinate the virtual\nworkspace does not serve, so the k8s verb was never reachable and the\ndiscovery client rendered the 403 as \"unknown\".\n\nRead the declaration from the hub catalog and accept all of it, which is\nwhat the portal and `railgrid dev` already do. A hardcoded list stops\nmatching spec.requires the moment a requirement is added, which is how\nthis test came to enable a kind without the verb on it.\n\n* Read the e2e bootstrap logs before cleanup deletes them\n\nThe tail added for the infrastructure provider e2e ran after cleanup(),\nwhich removes the whole data dir, so the failure reported\n\n  provider init failed: exit status 1 (log: /tmp/.../init.log)\n  (open /tmp/.../init.log: no such file or directory)\n\nTake the tail first. Give the serve readiness check the same treatment:\nits log is in the same directory and would be just as gone.\n\n* Claim the infrastructure Templates App Studio reads\n\nProject details failed with:\n\n  templates.infrastructure.railgrid.ai is forbidden: User\n  \"system:serviceaccount:default:provider\" cannot list resource\n  \"templates\" in API group \"infrastructure.railgrid.ai\" at the cluster\n  scope: access denied\n\nApp Studio reads that catalog in three places — preparing a project''s\ndetail view, resolving the template a binding names, and the assistant''s\ntemplate tool — but spec.requires named only instances and its verb\ncoordinates, so the generated claim never covered the kind and kcp served\nnothing for it. Declare it read-only.\n\nAudited every provider for the same class both ways a GVR is spelled in\nthis tree, the composite literal and GroupVersion.WithResource: no other\nkind is read from a group its provider does not declare. The one other\ncross-group read, agents reading the workspace''s MCPServer, is deliberate\n— it runs as the CALLER, on their bearer, so it needs no claim.\n\n* Revendor kcp at the custom-subresource parent gate\n\nmjudeikis/kcp 3b4bd7a70 (\"fix getter\"), one commit on from ba9e0a6a4.\nIt adds gateOnParent to the APIExport virtual workspace''s custom\nsubresource storage: before a verb runs, the object it hangs off is read\nback through the storage that serves the parent, label selector and all,\nso a claimer cannot reach a subresource of an object its claim does not\ncover.\n\nThat makes the parent claim load-bearing at request time rather than only\nat APIExport admission. Every verb coordinate this repo declares already\nsits under a claimed parent, including the code.railgrid.ai/connections\none added earlier in this branch, so the gate has an object to read in\neach case.\n\nAll twelve pins move together: the six replace targets in the root module\nplus the apimachinery/v2 pin the SDK and four providers carry. Every\nmodule builds and its tests pass.\n\n* rebase\n\n* Run the infrastructure provider e2e init as the provider, not as admin\n\nThe suite bootstrapped with kcp''s admin kubeconfig, and on this branch''s\nkcp that is refused:\n\n  init: provider workspace bootstrap: install: apply APIExport: creating\n  APIExport infrastructure.providers.railgrid.ai is forbidden:\n  spec.resources[0].group: Forbidden: API group\n  \"infrastructure.railgrid.ai\" is reserved by PermissionClaimPolicy\n  \"railgrid\"; only its providers may export it\n\nThe platform''s PermissionClaimPolicy reserves every API group it names and\nlists the subjects that may export one, and kcp-admin is not among them.\nmain never hit this because main binds upstream kcp v0.33.0, which has no\nsuch admission.\n\nMint the provider ServiceAccount''s kubeconfig from the provider-token\nSecret the hub''s Provider controller publishes, and hand init that. It is\nwhat `make init-provider-infrastructure` and the chart''s init container\nalready do, and what every other provider suite already does; this suite\nwas the only one reading no provider-token at all.\n\n* Treat an unresolved admin virtual workspace as an absent API\n\nThe External KCP suite deploys the hub against a released kcp image\n(ghcr.io/kcp-dev/kcp:v0.33.0, pinned in create_kcp.go), while the hub\nbinary is built from the vendored fork. The hub crash-looped there for 45\nminutes until Helm''s wait expired:\n\n  Error: installing PermissionClaimPolicy: discovering admin.kcp.io/v1alpha1:\n  forbidden: User \"railgrid-e2e-admin\" cannot get path\n  \"/services/admin/clusters/root/apis/admin.kcp.io/v1alpha1\":\n  Path not resolved to a valid virtual workspace\n\nPermissionClaimPolicyServed is meant to make this a no-op — its comment\nsays one info log on every kcp that does not serve admin.kcp.io, which is\ntoday''s — and it tolerated NotFound and a group-discovery failure. But the\ngroup lives behind a virtual workspace, and a path no virtual workspace\nclaims comes back 403: the framework''s authorizer has no opinion on a path\nit cannot resolve, and no opinion becomes a denial. So absence arrives as\nForbidden, which was neither tolerated case, and the caller treats a\nreturned error as fatal.\n\nTolerate that one shape, matched on the reason rather than on Forbidden\nalone: a denial from a kcp that does serve the group is a credential\nproblem, and reading it as absence would silently skip installing a policy\nwhose job is to reserve API groups.\n\n* Revendor kcp with the subresource path fix\n\nmjudeikis/kcp 20f1d300c. The APIExport virtual workspace now forwards the\npath a client addressed below a custom subresource, instead of carrying\nover only the query.\n\nThat is what the kuery edge aggregation needed. kuery reaches an edge''s\nKubernetes API through the k8s verb on kubernetesclusters, so every request\nis \"<edge>/k8s/<kube path>\". Inbound the virtual workspace saw\n.../kuery-k8s/k8s/apis/apiextensions.k8s.io/v1/customresourcedefinitions;\noutbound it sent .../kubernetesclusters:<identity>/kuery-k8s/k8s?watch=true.\nWith no tail the edges provider resolves /k8s/, the agent proxies the edge\napiserver''s root, and the root answers 200 with its paths document -- so\nclient-go reported \"Object ''Kind'' is missing\" and the CRD informer never\nsynced. Nothing else caught it because every other path through the k8s\nverb goes via the shard, which preserves the inbound path.\n\nAll twelve pins move together. Every module builds and its tests pass.\n\n* Report why a provider e2e bootstrap failed, in every suite\n\nThe kuery provider suite failed with\n\n  kuery init failed: exit status 1 (log: /tmp/railgrid-e2e-kuery-.../init.log)\n\nand that directory is removed by cleanup and never uploaded, so the reason\nwas gone. The infrastructure suite had the same blindness and it cost three\nCI rounds to read one admission error.\n\nTail the log to stderr, taken before cleanup, in the four suites that still\nhid it: edges, edgesconn, kueryprovider and provider.\n\n* Tell the kuery provider e2e where its data plane is\n\n  init: provider workspace bootstrap: install: DataPlaneEndpointSlice: no\n  data-plane base URL (set Options.DataPlaneURL, or point\n  Options.CatalogEntryFile at a CatalogEntry with spec.serving.backend.url)\n\nkuery''s APIExport declares \"<resource>/<verb>\" entries, so init writes the\nDataPlaneEndpointSlice they resolve through, and it refuses to guess the\naddress. The suite deliberately gave init no CatalogEntry, because it\nregisters the entry itself.\n\nPass the address directly, as the quickstart and infrastructure suites do.\nIt is the one applyKueryManifests already rewrites spec.serving.backend.url\nto, so the slice and the entry agree on where the provider is; reading the\ncommitted manifest instead would record the dev-loop port.\n\n* Report what the provider said when the edge-proxy gate refuses\n\nTestDEdgeProxyAuthBoundary fails with\n\n  wait timeout after 30s; last status: status=404 (want 502)\n\nand 404 is what the gate answers for every refusal, deliberately: a denial\nmust not disclose whether the addressed edge exists. So the status cannot\nsay whether the caller was denied, the object was unreadable as the\nprovider, or the review never ran, and the three have different causes.\n\nKeep the provider log path in suite state and dump its tail when the probe\nnever reaches 502.\n\n* Name the hop that refused the edge-proxy probe\n\nThe provider log tail showed only startup, because one line in these logs can\nbe a whole API object, so forty lines cover a few milliseconds. The useful\nfact was in what was absent: nothing in the provider log mentions the edge\nthe probe addresses, so the 404 comes from before the provider and the gate\nis not what refused.\n\nMatch on the edge name instead of tailing, over the hub''s log as well as the\nprovider''s, so the next run says which hop answered.\n\n* Forward a ServiceAccount request to the workspace it addresses\n\nTestDEdgeProxyAuthBoundary read 404 where it wanted 502, before and after\nthe grant, and nothing in the edges provider''s log ever mentioned the edge\nthe probe addresses: the request never got past kcp. The hub''s proxy was\nsending it to a path that cannot exist.\n\n  inbound    /clusters/{tenant}/apis/edges.railgrid.ai/v1alpha1/\n             kubernetesclusters/e2e-engage/k8s/api\n  forwarded  /clusters/{sa}/clusters/{tenant}/apis/...\n\nserveServiceAccount resolves the workspace from the token''s clusterName\nclaim, which is where the ServiceAccount LIVES, not where the request is\naimed. It de-doubled the prefix only when the path named the SA''s own\ncluster, so a request addressing another workspace -- which a data-plane\nverb on another provider''s object always does -- got a second prefix\nprepended. main never hit this because the probe took the old grammar,\nwhich carried no cluster prefix.\n\nHonour a cluster named in the path and forward it unchanged. That is safe\nbecause the SA token travels as it arrived: kcp authenticates it natively\nand authorizes it in THAT workspace, so reaching another one still needs a\ngrant there, which is what this test grants. Both checks the claim gets --\nthe traversal regex and the O-10 Org refusal -- are applied to the\naddressed cluster too, so naming one in the path walks around neither. The\nagent-kubeconfig case the old strip existed for falls out of the same\nbranch.","tree":{"sha":"158326845ee91bb47e5822c3217146994ab70077","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/158326845ee91bb47e5822c3217146994ab70077"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDFlZjhiYTA0YTU3ZjA2ZGVkZGJmY2Y0YjQ4MDlhMTM2NmU0MzM2Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626","sha":"deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626"}],"sha":"1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/1ef8ba04a57f06deddbfcf4b4809a1366e433667"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5685031?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T23:11:34Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T23:11:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add shared table multi-selection and bulk settings actions (#775)\n\n* Add resource table selection and bulk workspace deletion\n\n* Polish resource selection toolbar and tooltip behavior\n\n* Clarify selection toolbar placement in the table contract\n\n* Preserve focus when clearing off-page resource selection\n\n* Fix resource selection layout, focus, and live tooltip updates\n\n* Keep cleared selection focus visible and fit narrow toolbars\n\n* Fix table action tooltip clipping and progress animation\n\n* Add bulk actions to workspace settings resource tables\n\n* Add organization member bulk removal and compact empty tables\n\n* Preserve retries for incomplete organization member removals\n\n* Fix bulk settings stack CI dependencies and bundle budgets","tree":{"sha":"1c9a7ca27e6f1edea662226b2a80b1e60ccd9447","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/1c9a7ca27e6f1edea662226b2a80b1e60ccd9447"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKGRlYWYzNWZkZjA0ZTUyMmM0ZDMxNTBmODcxOTI5MDllMGJlYzA2MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f","sha":"3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f"}],"sha":"deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/deaf35fdf04e522c4d3150f87192909e0bec0626"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5685031?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T23:11:33Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T23:11:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Simplify workspace navigation and settings creation flows (#774)\n\n* Simplify workspace creation and settings navigation\n\n* Fix workspace creation handoff and align organization settings\n\n* Clarify workspace and organization membership scopes\n\n* Standardize settings lists on PortalKit resource tables\n\n* Fix spacing between settings forms and resource tables\n\n* Move settings member and service account creation into modals\n\n* Fix settings creation feedback and service account progress\n\n* Fix App Studio bundle budget for shared busy actions","tree":{"sha":"b2f09f42a5b6f5878c8db96999c1d538b0643394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/b2f09f42a5b6f5878c8db96999c1d538b0643394"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDNmYmMxYTZjY2ZiYjU0YThiZTk3ZmQwMDhiM2M0OWQ2NDJmMTg5NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f","sha":"9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f"}],"sha":"3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/3fbc1a6ccfbb54a8be97fd008b3c49d642f1895f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:55:45Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:55:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Provider contract review (#769)\n\n* Provider contract hardenining\n\n* extend providers sdk with serve\n\n* rework apiexport cross-claims\n\n* fix duplicate hash\n\n* Rework provider integrations\n\n* e2e test\n\n* Fix Ci\n\n* fix more CI\n\n* Fix broken features","tree":{"sha":"48d6eaec93d802a9a064022096ad7997d74f3e0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/48d6eaec93d802a9a064022096ad7997d74f3e0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDlhMGU3N2YwZTA3Y2IzOThlOThiODBlZDA5NTQ2YWY2OWU2NGE0NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3","sha":"708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3"}],"sha":"9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/9a0e77f0e07cb398e98b80ed09546af69e64a44f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:36:02Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:36:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Drive provider flows with reconcilers and watches instead of timers (#766)\n\n* Refresh runner sources from origin and harden add-on permissions\n\nThe local runner now refreshes a source checkout from its own origin when\nan approved commit is missing (a base branch that moved on after a merge),\nusing the operator''s Git credentials with hooks disabled, and only then\nserves the isolated task clone from it. fetchRemoteURL becomes the\nfallback for sources without a usable origin. The add-on supervisor\nreclaims orphaned children on unix, linux and bsd hosts.\n\nEdge add-ons gain permissionMode and allowedTools so a coding runner can\nbe pinned to acceptEdits with an explicit shell allow list; CRDs and\nschemas are regenerated. The code provider''s GitHub backend treats only a\nmerged pull request as merge proof and verifies runner snapshot commits\nheader by header. App Studio''s assistant permission check pauses\npromote_project and hydrate_workspace in every approval mode short of\nNever.\n\n* Drive provider flows with reconcilers and watches instead of timers\n\nEvery provider polled internal platform state on a timer somewhere:\nreconcilers requeueing every 10 to 60 seconds to re-read objects they\ncould watch, HTTP handlers owning lifecycle state a reconciler also\nwrote, and one provider with no reconcilers at all. Only external\nsystems (GitHub, LLM APIs, helm, edge devices over the tunnel) should be\npolled; everything else now converges on watches.\n\nagents: a leader-elected multicluster-runtime manager on the agents\nAPIExport runs Schedule, Connection and Agent reconcilers in place of the\n30s CR scan. Schedule fires via RequeueAfter and a conflict-checked\nstatus claim; Connection owns Slack/Telegram secret repair, OAuth refresh\nat expiry and Discord session state, with a Secret watch. Runs stay in\nPostgres by design; cancellation is durable through a cancel_requested\ncolumn the engine checks before every model round and tool call, and\nevery submit path persists a Pending row before enqueueing.\n\nedges: the lifecycle reconciler is the single writer of Edge\nconnected/phase/lastHeartbeatTime, derived from the tunnel-registry\nLease and triggered by a Lease watch and connection-manager events, so\nit is correct at any replica count. The tunnel handler and the\nagent-side reporter no longer write those fields. The addon reconciler\nwatches its token Secret; the scheduler drops its unconditional 30s\nrequeue.\n\ninfrastructure: the Instance reconciler watches runtime-cluster CRs\n(registered per Template GVR), Templates and tenant Secrets instead of\n10s/60s/3s requeues; runtime CRs carry cluster and instance annotations\nso events map back. The Template reconciler watches RGDs so kro\nrejection surfaces in BackendReady.\n\napp-studio: Project and Studio reconcilers watch Repository,\nRepositoryCommit and Instance objects through each workspace''s own\nbindings; the in-memory pending-commit map becomes a Project annotation\nbacked by a workspace ledger; sandbox readiness and deletion use a single\nwatch; Session status is signalled by the supervisor on turn transitions\ninstead of a 30s Postgres poll.\n\ncode: MCP tools wait on a watch instead of a 1s GET loop; Collaborator\nrequeues while a GitHub invitation is pending.\n\nkuery: KubernetesClusters are watched per workspace through the\nworkspace''s own edges binding; the 20s requeue remains only as the Lease\nheartbeat.\n\nNo cross-provider permission claims were added: they pin one identity\nhash and break when an org self-hosts a provider (see ed0766f8).\n\n* update agent.md\n\n* refrence in providers\n\n* Fix CI: hydrate test race, agents image build, containerd advisory\n\nThe hydrate tool test read its sync-action record while the scheduled\nsync goroutine was still appending to it; the record is now guarded and\nthe test waits for the first call. The agents image build copied an\nexplicit directory list that predates the controllers, scheme and\ninternal packages, so it now copies the whole module like the code\nprovider. containerd moves to 1.7.35 in the root and edges modules for\nGO-2026-6444, which the vulnerability gate started reporting on\n2026-09-16.","tree":{"sha":"44979279f7888c5b1344e98b25d924e04efc8910","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/44979279f7888c5b1344e98b25d924e04efc8910"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDcwOGZhMDQyZDc2Mjc0ZThmNmRmYmZhNWZhYmJmNTU4NGZiZjFlZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca","sha":"d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca"}],"sha":"708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/708fa042d76274e8f6dfbfa5fabbf5584fbf1ed3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5685031?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:03:05Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:03:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add shared collapsible resource boards and align resource headings (#762)\n\n* Align shared resource headings with dense typography standard\n\n* Add shared resource board with discoverable empty columns\n\n* Align AgentKit assertion with board stylesheet version\n\n* Keep hidden board columns compact and record validation","tree":{"sha":"ca98588872a5e31331bfce5b23be2513972cdda9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/ca98588872a5e31331bfce5b23be2513972cdda9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKGQxNTk1MTg3ZGM1NGZmYmQ4NTY2MTY1NzMwNjc5NzkxM2Q5MGY1Y2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd","sha":"a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd"}],"sha":"d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/d1595187dc54ffbd85661657306797913d90f5ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T11:11:41Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T11:11:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Remove deprecated CLI commands and always write endpoint slice export paths (#751)\n\n* Remove deprecated CLI spellings\n\nThe rename dropped the need for backwards compatibility, so remove the\nhidden pre-1.0 commands and fallbacks:\n- `railgrid get` and `railgrid apply` (use kubectl or `railgrid edge list`)\n- `railgrid kubeconfig edge` (use `railgrid edge kubeconfig`)\n- the hidden `railgrid list`/`ls` shorthand (use `railgrid edge list`)\n- `railgrid dev create --agent-count` (use `--worker-count`)\n- login treating a non-JSON /healthz as an old server with OIDC; it is\n  now an error\n- the unused SaveAgentConfig wrapper\n\nUpdate docs, skills, the edges portal, hub hints and e2e tests to the\ncurrent spellings.\n\n* Always write the export path on APIExportEndpointSlices\n\nA path-less slice is indexed only under its logical-cluster name, so a\nshard''s endpoint-URL publisher, which looks slices up by the binding''s\ncanonical export path, misses it and never publishes its virtual\nworkspace URL for the first binding on another shard. Resolve the\nworkspace path from the LogicalCluster when none is configured and\nalways write it; path-less slices from older SDKs are recreated once.\n\n* Use the install script in the portal CLI quickstart\n\n* Drop removed CLI spellings from the e2e suites\n\nThe CLI suite still expected the hidden ''railgrid ls'' and the edges\nconnectivity suite still called ''railgrid kubeconfig edge''.","tree":{"sha":"9b6a1ab4e9a1dcccf589bef3870bb3f268263517","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/9b6a1ab4e9a1dcccf589bef3870bb3f268263517"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKGE4ZjdiNjkxOTBiYWEyMzExMDZhZWU1YTA4YzVlNjIwNjJlMmViZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/1dab5d6864091f2f808fb8685d268a5034c7e330","sha":"1dab5d6864091f2f808fb8685d268a5034c7e330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/1dab5d6864091f2f808fb8685d268a5034c7e330"}],"sha":"a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/a8f7b69190baa231106aee5a08c5e62062e2ebfd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/1dab5d6864091f2f808fb8685d268a5034c7e330/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:23:09Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:23:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump kcp to v0.33.0 and kcp-operator to v0.10.0 (#750)\n\n* Bump kcp to v0.33.0 and kcp-operator to v0.10.0\n\nMove every Go module to kcp v0.33.0 (sdk, client-go, cli,\nvirtual-workspace-framework, apimachinery/v2 v2.33.0) and drop the\nmjudeikis/kcp fork replaces; the fork carried kcp#4280, which ships in\nv0.33.0.\n\nAdapt the infrastructure provider to two v0.33 API breaks:\n- CachedResource is renamed to ClusterCachedResource (kcp#4281)\n- APIExport storage.virtual.identityHash is removed (kcp#4326)\n\nPoint local setups at the releases: Tiltfile.cluster defaults to the\nv0.33.0 image, `railgrid dev create kcp` uses chart 0.16.6 with the\nv0.33.0 image, the Makefile kcp binary and apigen move to v0.33.0, the\nexternal install defaults to kcp-operator v0.10.0, and tilt-e2e checks\nout kcp v0.33.0.\n\n* Align kcp apimachinery replaces on v2.33.0 across modules\n\nprovider-sdk, app-studio and code still replaced apimachinery/v2 with\nv2.32.0, which conflicts with the root module in the CI go.work.","tree":{"sha":"cfefd865369bdb980b3079db3fdc4fe114efae52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/cfefd865369bdb980b3079db3fdc4fe114efae52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/1dab5d6864091f2f808fb8685d268a5034c7e330","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/1dab5d6864091f2f808fb8685d268a5034c7e330","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDFkYWI1ZDY4NjQwOTFmMmY4MDhmYjg2ODVkMjY4YTUwMzRjN2UzMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"htt