/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/0a7811cd4dff3910672a15eb6854881b4ec13a88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T07:54:55Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T07:54:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump providers sdk (#509)\n\n* Bump providers sdk\n\n* Quote context name in kubectl hint output\n\nCo-authored-by: mjudeikis <3225744+mjudeikis@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: mjudeikis <3225744+mjudeikis@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e10060c868434ad0f94e0c169f45ade968b2e2a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/e10060c868434ad0f94e0c169f45ade968b2e2a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/0a7811cd4dff3910672a15eb6854881b4ec13a88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/0a7811cd4dff3910672a15eb6854881b4ec13a88","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDBhNzgxMWNkNGRmZjM5MTA2NzJhMTVlYjY4NTQ4ODFiNGVjMTNhODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775","sha":"88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775"}],"sha":"0a7811cd4dff3910672a15eb6854881b4ec13a88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/0a7811cd4dff3910672a15eb6854881b4ec13a88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:35:10Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:35:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rename kedge → faros across the entire repo (#507)\n\n* Rename kedge -> faros across the entire repo\n\nThe project has always lived under the faros.sh domain while the code called\nitself kedge. This collapses the two: there is no kedge.faros.sh any more,\nonly faros.sh.\n\nMechanical, case-preserving rename with these ordered rules:\n\n  faros-kedge       -> faros           (module path)\n  kedge_faros_sh    -> faros_sh        (GraphQL-mangled group identifiers)\n  KedgeFarosSh      -> FarosSh         (GraphQL type prefixes)\n  kedge.faros.sh    -> faros.sh        (API groups; before the generic rule)\n  KEDGE/Kedge/kedge -> FAROS/Faros/faros\n\nWhat that covers:\n  - module github.com/faroshq/faros-kedge -> github.com/faroshq/faros\n  - API groups *.kedge.faros.sh -> *.faros.sh; the root group is now faros.sh\n  - env vars KEDGE_* -> FAROS_* (hard cut, no compatibility aliases)\n  - HTTP headers X-Kedge-* -> X-Faros-*\n  - template tokens ${kedge.devImage.*} -> ${faros.*}, kedgeMode -> farosMode\n  - images ghcr.io/faroshq/kedge-* -> faros-*; charts faros-hub / faros-agent\n  - dirs apis/kedge, cmd/kedge{,-hub,-release}, deploy/charts/kedge-*\n  - generated CRDs/APIExports/APIResourceSchemas renamed in content and filename\n    (text-renamed, not regenerated)\n\nmarkEdgeConnected/markEdgeDisconnected are mark+Edge, not kedge, and are\ndeliberately left alone.\n\nThree changes are NOT a plain text substitution, because a substitution alone\nwould have been wrong:\n\n  - .github/workflows/images.yaml derived the hub and agent image names from\n    ${{ github.repository }}, which would have kept publishing kedge-hub and\n    kedge-agent while every chart pulls faros-hub/faros-agent. They are now\n    spelled out as repository_owner + a literal name, matching helm-images.yaml\n    and the provider matrix.\n  - The application/simple-webapp templates embed the Vite dev shim as a base64\n    payload, which a text pass cannot see into. It still imported\n    file:///kedge/bin/preview-console-plugin.mjs while the dev overlay now\n    mounts /faros/bin. Both payloads were decoded, renamed and re-encoded.\n  - The databricks assistant skill artifact records a content digest over the\n    skill text. Renaming the text changed the digest, so manifest.yaml and the\n    chart catalogentry now carry the recomputed value.\n\nVerified: go vet and go test (excluding cluster-backed e2e) are clean across all\neleven modules plus the linux-only dev-agent. Every changed file other than the\nthree cases above was re-derived from its parent revision by reapplying the\nrules and byte-compared, so the rest of the diff is provably the rename and\nnothing else.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* templates: pin scaffolds to v0.1.3\n\nfaros-scaffold-application and faros-scaffold-simple-webapp were renamed from\nkedge-scaffold-* and re-tagged v0.1.3 with the same rename applied inside.\n\nThe published image path follows GITHUB_REPOSITORY, so the repo rename moved\npublishing to ghcr.io/faroshq/faros-scaffold-*. The v0.1.2 tag only ever\nexisted under the old kedge-scaffold-* package names, so the renamed template\nreferences would have 404''d until this bump — nothing re-publishes an old tag\nunder a new package name.\n\nBumps together, as the templates require: the scaffold git refs and the\nsampleValues/default image tags.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix two rename fallouts caught by CI: escaped-regex group and gofmt\n\nNeither was visible to the text substitution or to go vet/go test locally.\n\n1. The Template instanceCRD.group validator is a regex with ESCAPED dots:\n\n     ^infrastructure\\.kedge\\.faros\\.sh$\n\n   The `kedge.faros.sh -> faros.sh` rule matches the literal group string, so\n   it never fired on the escaped form; the generic `kedge -> faros` rule then\n   produced `^infrastructure\\.faros\\.faros\\.sh$`. Every Template was rejected\n   at admission, which is why the infraprovider e2e suite could not seed its\n   catalog. Fixed in the kubebuilder marker and both generated CRD copies.\n\n   Swept for the same failure in every other encoding (\\. . - _ and\n   concatenated): the only other hits are `faros-faros-hub`, which is helm''s\n   <release>-<chart> naming and was `kedge-kedge-hub` before — correct as is.\n\n2. Shortening the group strings changed the width of aligned trailing\n   comments, so gofmt reformatted 15 files. Alignment only, no code change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* providers: build against the in-tree provider-sdk\n\nThe providers require published provider-sdk versions (v0.0.1/v0.0.8/v0.0.13)\nwith no replace, so only go.work made them compile against this repo''s copy.\nCI has no go.work, so it silently linked the PUBLISHED SDK instead — which is\nstill pre-rename and writes ClusterRole \"kedge:providers:bind:<export>\". The\nprovider e2e suite asserts the renamed \"faros:providers:bind:<export>\" and\nfailed on exactly that, reproducibly in CI and never locally.\n\nsplit-provider-sdk.yaml''s own header already describes this arrangement —\n\"providers depend on this SDK via replace => ../../provider-sdk in the\nmonorepo\" — it had just never been applied. Adding it makes CI match local and\nkeeps the SDK in lockstep with the rename instead of straddling a published\nboundary mid-rename.\n\ngo mod tidy on agents, app-studio, infrastructure, kuery and vibe-studio: the\nin-tree SDK''s dependency set differs from the v0.0.1 they had pinned.\n\nVerified the way CI builds (GOWORK=off): all nine providers compile, and the\nquickstart binary now carries only \"faros:providers:bind:\" — no kedge string\nsurvives in the linked SDK.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* e2e: run provider suites against the in-tree provider-sdk\n\nReverts the per-provider `replace => ../../provider-sdk` added in b03a416b and\nfixes the underlying problem in CI instead.\n\nThe replace was wrong. go.work.template and hack/provider-sdk-cutover.sh both\nrecord that those replaces were deliberately DROPPED once the SDK was\npublished, and each provider Dockerfile says so too (\"uses the published\nfaros-provider-sdk (no replace), fetched from the proxy\"). Provider images\nbuild with the provider directory as the Docker context, so ../../provider-sdk\nis outside the context and every provider image build failed with\n\"reading /provider-sdk/go.mod: no such file or directory\".\n\nThe real issue is narrower: the provider e2e suites build provider binaries and\nassert on their behaviour, so they must exercise THIS commit''s SDK. Workspace\nmode is how the monorepo develops the SDK and its consumers together, but\ngo.work is gitignored, so CI never had one and silently linked the published\nSDK — which is pre-rename and writes \"kedge:providers:bind:<export>\" while the\nsuite asserts the renamed \"faros:providers:bind:<export>\". That is why it failed\nonly in CI and never locally.\n\nThe e2e job now builds the workspace before running, leaving go.mod, the\npublished-module contract and the image builds untouched.\n\nNote for after merge: provider IMAGES still link the last published provider-sdk\n(v0.0.1/v0.0.8/v0.0.13), so they keep writing kedge-prefixed bind ClusterRoles\nuntil provider-sdk is re-tagged from this branch and each provider''s require is\nbumped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d07eaf0726a80cf07291c814ce7ded0f6f0392f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/3d07eaf0726a80cf07291c814ce7ded0f6f0392f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDg4ZTllMDFiMzU2MWJlNjI3MTM5MTNhMGJmZjdmMjAxODMxODU3NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9","sha":"cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9"}],"sha":"88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/88e9e01b3561be62713913a0bff7f20183185775"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5685031?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T23:29:50Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T23:29:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add Provider Actions and Databricks-backed App Studio integrations (#499)\n\n* Improve App Studio execution and verification flows\n\n* Improve application studio execution and UI flows\n\n* Improve application studio workflow and runtime state handling\n\n* Harden App Studio provider action recovery\n\n* move provider actions to virtual-workspace\n\n* remove committed kind kubeconfig and ignore stray root-level dumps\n\nThe extension-less file ''tilt'' was a kind-cluster kubeconfig carrying a\nclient private key; *.kubeconfig was already ignored but nothing caught\nfiles without the extension.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* rework menu & few fixes\n\n* Centralize Provider Actions runtime binding overlays\n\n* Relax App Studio no-progress termination\n\n* Preserve read evidence during App Studio context reduction\n\n* port browser to infra\n\n* clean old browser workers\n\n* Stabilize App Studio integration runtime\n\n* Fix dev-agent image build context\n\n* Improve App Studio project creation flow and preview diagnostics\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4886f77ae86c8e8b3b82c4bf5755032b3f811c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/4886f77ae86c8e8b3b82c4bf5755032b3f811c6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKGNkMTZiMjNlZDk0NGRiZjg0ZjY4ZmYyYjkyMmFhNGM2MWFjYjc5Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b","sha":"bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b"}],"sha":"cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/cd16b23ed944dbf84f68ff2b922aa4c61acb79b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T06:55:01Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T06:55:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"app-studio: vibe-studio engine retrofit + creation wizard, code explorer, edit-reliability fixes (#500)\n\n* Retrofit vibe to app\n\n* app-studio: vibe-studio engine retrofit + creation wizard, code explorer, edit-reliability fixes\n\nApp Studio now runs the vibe-studio engine model end to end:\n\nReconcilers & permissions\n- Multicluster APIExport Project reconciler lifecycles instances from self-contained\n  bindings; Session CR (Postgres projection + purge finalizer) and Studio singleton\n  (shared searxng web search) reconcilers; per-project ServiceAccount identity.\n- Handlers inverted to spec-only writes; instances/repos/commits converge in-loop.\n- Permission claims: infra instances + repositories + searxngs + serviceaccounts/\n  secrets/RBAC, with infra/code identity hashes (init_cmd + manifest + catalogentry\n  + chart + Makefile auto-discovery).\n\nScaffolding & wizard-first creation\n- Templates'' spec.development.scaffold seeds the workspace at template bind (repo =\n  scaffold); tracked as uncommitted so commit convergence + dev-sync pick it up.\n- Blueprint-first creation: /api/projects/plan + SSE /api/projects/stream surface\n  live steps (\"Attaching scaffold to <template>\"); NewProjectWizard is the default\n  landing flow.\n- Code workbench tab: read-only explorer of the live dev workspace\n  (/files + /files/content + CodeExplorer.vue).\n\nEdit-reliability fixes (root-caused via run-event forensics)\n- Mutation gate uses the recorded complete-read version instead of the model''s\n  fabricated token; read limit is clamped, not rejected.\n- Context reduction no longer leaves empty tool-call objects the model imitated.\n- Commit convergence no longer aborted by transient instance update conflicts.\n- Promote guard refuses while the workspace is dirty.\n\nAlso carries shared portalkit (toast) + design-system updates across providers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* app-studio: meaningful auto-commit messages from the reconciler\n\nThe commit-convergence loop wrote \"chore: sync workspace (N files)\", which\nsays nothing about the change. Build the message from the actual paths:\nsubject names the file for a single change, or the count + top-level areas\n(e.g. \"Update 3 files, delete 1 file in web, api\") for many; the body lists\nthe paths. Deterministic, no coupling to the assistant layer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"273981fa0032f83dfd6f917fdb6583d660bc0368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/273981fa0032f83dfd6f917fdb6583d660bc0368"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKGJkODg1Njc0MzhlNzljNDQ1NjM0MDdhMDVlZTlkNzZhNTI5N2FmM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b","sha":"b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b"}],"sha":"bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/bd88567438e79c44563407a05ee9d76a5297af3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:57:21Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:57:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Agents bigbang (#484)\n\n* Agents big bang. part 1\n\n* agents.search\n\n* feat(infrastructure,agents): platform-internal networking for tenant workloads\n\nAgents could only reach a self-hosted searxng/browser instance over a public\nHTTPRoute, because no internal path existed. Everything built to make that\nsafe — an nginx bearer sidecar, a token bridge copying the agents Connection\nSecret into the runtime namespace, an `allowedHosts` SSRF opt-in in the UI —\nwas compensating for a missing capability, and it still did not work in Tilt\nwhere the provider runs on the host and the gateway has only cluster-internal\naddresses.\n\nThe platform already had the path: the infrastructure provider''s data plane,\nwhich proxies through the runtime apiserver''s services/proxy subresource. It\nonly lacked a `proxy` verb declaration on these templates.\n\nTemplates now declare a dataPlane proxy verb over their Service, and a\nwebsearch/mcp Connection names `config.instance` instead of a URL and a token.\nThe call authenticates as the calling user; the data plane authorizes by\nre-reading the instance as that caller, so kcp RBAC on the instance is the\nwhole gate and the workload holds no credential. Deleted: the HTTPRoute-always\nposture, the nginx sidecar, tokenbridge.go and its finalizer, and the\ntokenSecretRef/tokenSecretName inputs.\n\nPublic exposure survives as an opt-in for humans with a browser, gated by\noauth2-proxy — reusing the `application` template''s existing gate and OIDC\nclient-secret bridge rather than resurrecting a shared bearer token.\nexpose.enabled defaults to false; every exposure resource hangs off that one\ncondition so the route can never outlive its gate; oidc.mode=none is not\noffered, since these apps have no auth of their own.\n\nTemplates also declare `spec.exposure` (internal|optional|public), surfaced in\nlist_templates, describe_template and the portal catalog, so callers stop\npolling status.url for an instance that will never have one. The kro backend\nrejects a marker that contradicts the graph.\n\nKnown limitation: scheduled/background/channel runs carry no user token and so\ncannot use an instance-backed tool. They fail with an explicit message rather\nthan a 401 two hops away; closing it needs provider identity.\n\nTests: data-plane URL composition and its failure messages; the query string\nsurviving the proxy rewrite (search puts its whole request there, so dropping\nit would read as \"no results\"); the exposure marker vs the graph; the OIDC\ngate matrix; and that every run path wires ClusterID + HubToken — a gap the\ninteractive chat path had, which broke search in the one place it must work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(portalkit): lift the modal accessibility fix into the canonical source\n\nThe agents portal''s vendored copy of modal.ts carried a focus trap, a\ndialog-scoped keydown handler and the removal of a global Enter-confirms\nhandler — with a note saying it had to be lifted back upstream. It never was,\nso verify-portalkit went red: the copy no longer matched provider-sdk.\n\nSyncing would have \"fixed\" CI by deleting the fix and restoring the bug it\nwas written for — a global Enter handler that fired a destructive confirm no\nmatter where focus was. So the fix moves the other way: into\nprovider-sdk/portalkit, then re-synced. The kuery and quickstart portals\ninherit it too, which is the point of the shared kit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(agents/portal): retire the assisted-search card once it has been used\n\nThe card offering \"set up self-hosted search with an agent\" rendered on every\nvisit to Connections, forever — including for workspaces that set search up\nweeks ago. An onboarding shortcut that never retires is just clutter.\n\nIt now hides when a self-hosted search connection already exists. Because the\nflow creates that Connection as its FIRST step, the card disappears as soon as\nthe user completes the dialog rather than waiting for the instance to finish\nprovisioning. A Brave connection does not count: that is search, but not the\nself-hosted search this card offers.\n\nIt can also be dismissed by hand, remembered per WORKSPACE — search set up in\none workspace says nothing about another, and a single dismissal must not hide\nthe affordance everywhere. Storage access is wrapped: private-browsing modes\nthrow, and degrading to a per-session dismissal beats white-screening.\n\nThe card also waits for the connections slice to load before deciding, so\nusers who finished onboarding no longer get a flash of it on every page load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(infrastructure): status.url must derive from a resource, not from spec\n\nRegression from the optional-exposure change: searxng and browser gained\n\n  url: ${schema.spec.expose.enabled ? \"https://\" + schema.spec.expose.fqdn : \"\"}\n\nwhich this kro fork rejects outright — it builds the instance status schema\nwithout the spec in scope, so the RGD lands GraphAccepted=False with\n\"references unknown identifiers: [schema]\" and the template never becomes\nready. Both templates were rejected in the E2E; searxng.yaml''s own comment\nwarned about this rule and I introduced exactly what it warned against.\n\nFixed by using the idiom application.yaml and simple-webapp.yaml already use —\nderive from the HTTPRoute:\n\n  url: ${\"https://\" + httpRoute.spec.hostnames[0] + \"${kedge.appPublicPort}\"}\n\nwhich happens to give the wanted semantics for free: the route is\nincludeWhen-gated, so the field resolves only for an instance that opted into\nexposure and is simply absent otherwise. The dev overlay already relies on\nthis (status.runtimeNamespace references the mode-gated dev control Secret),\nand those E2E subtests pass.\n\nbuildRGD now rejects ${schema.*} in a status mapping, so the next author gets\nan immediate message naming the field and the alternative instead of an opaque\nkro rejection eight minutes into an E2E run. One dev-overlay test fixture was\nauthoring a status value real kro would have rejected; it now uses a resource\nreference.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e27f63709f38cb8a4e0c3bc248fb2a550016ac9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/e27f63709f38cb8a4e0c3bc248fb2a550016ac9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKGIyMmU2YTQ0N2Y2M2M4ZTc1NDhiY2RmYmZhYjFkM2JhMTA2OGZmN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab","sha":"19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab"}],"sha":"b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/b22e6a447f63c8e7548bcdfbfab1d3ba1068ff7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:02:28Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:02:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(portals): shared portalkit — icons, in-page modals, tables, tenant plumbing (#466)\n\n* feat(portalkit): shared vendored UI kit (icons + in-page modal) + CI drift guard\n\nExternalize the agents portal''s icon set into a canonical, copy-synced kit so\nthe vanilla-TS provider portals (agents, kuery, quickstart) share ONE source of\ntruth without an npm workspace (builds stay self-contained per portal).\n\n- provider-sdk/portalkit/: canonical icons.ts (moved from agents) + new modal.ts\n  (promise-based confirmModal()/alertModal() replacing native window.confirm/\n  alert with an on-brand, token-themed in-page dialog).\n- hack/sync-portalkit.sh + `make sync-portalkit` vendor the kit into each\n  portal''s src/portalkit/; `make verify-portalkit` (wired into `make verify`\n  and a new CI job) fails on drift, mirroring verify-codegen.\n- agents portal now consumes the vendored copy and uses confirmModal() for all\n  11 destructive confirmations (delete agent/connection/toolset/schedule/\n  trigger/credential, reassign schedule/trigger) — no more native dialogs.\n\nVerified: agents typecheck + vite build clean; playwright 13/13 (main) + 7/7\n(models) + 4/4 (modal: in-page dialog opens danger-styled, cancel/escape\ndismiss, confirm fires the DELETE, zero native dialogs); provider-sdk go build\nclean; portalkit copies byte-identical across all four locations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(portals): finish glyph sweep (kuery/code/edges) + self-injecting icon styles\n\n- portalkit/icons.ts now self-injects its .ic sizing rule on import, so the\n  raw-CSS-injection portals get icon styling without wiring a stylesheet\n  (dropped the separate icons.css). Re-synced to all vanilla portals.\n- kuery: ''Run ▸'' → ic(''play'') (now consumes the shared portalkit).\n- code: ⚠ → <AlertTriangle> (RepoDetailView), and reword an input-value ✓.\n- edges: table ✓ → <Check> (Services).\n\nColorful emoji were already gone across every portal; these were the residual\nsymbol glyphs. Verified: kuery/code/edges typecheck + build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(portalkit-vue): shared Vue confirm dialog; migrate all portals off native confirm\n\nAdd the Vue half of the shared UI kit and finish removing native window.confirm/\nalert from every portal.\n\n- provider-sdk/portalkit-vue/: canonical confirm.ts (promise-based confirmDialog,\n  promoted from the code provider) + a self-contained ConfirmDialog.vue with\n  scoped, design-token styles so it drops into any Vue portal (Tailwind or plain\n  CSS). Synced by `make sync-portalkit` into all six Vue portals'' src/portalkit/.\n- Migrated the three portals still on native dialogs to the shared kit:\n  edges (5 sites, +mounted dialog), app-studio (3), root kedge-portal (10 across\n  TenantSettings/Providers/MCP).\n- Deduplicated code + databricks onto the shared kit and deleted their local\n  confirm.ts / ConfirmDialog.vue / ConfirmHost.vue copies.\n\nRepo-wide there are now ZERO native confirm/alert/prompt calls. Verified: every\ntouched portal (edges, app-studio, code, databricks, root) typechecks + vite\nbuilds clean; agents modal suite still 4/4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portalkit-vue): extract shared ResourceTable + ConditionsPanel + StatusBadge\n\nThe code and databricks portals shipped byte-identical ResourceTable.vue,\nConditionsPanel.vue and StatusBadge.vue (the repeated table markup + status\nbadges). Promote them to provider-sdk/portalkit-vue, sync into the Vue portals''\nsrc/portalkit/, repoint code + databricks, and delete the local copies.\n\nVerified: code + databricks typecheck + vite build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(portalkit): shared security-critical tenant plumbing + document the kit\n\nThe hub-proxy contract (tenant from localStorage + Authorization / X-Kedge-Org /\nX-Kedge-Workspace headers + /ui→/services rewrite) was re-inlined in every\nportal''s api.ts. Wrong header/key = 401/403, so it now lives in ONE canonical\nplace: provider-sdk/portalkit/tenant.ts (plain TS, synced to all portals).\n\n- readTenant(), tenantHeaders({token,json}), serviceBase() — exact behavior of\n  the previous inline copies.\n- Migrated the two exact hub-proxy matches: agents (ApiClient) and app-studio\n  (which had the header block duplicated twice within one file).\n- Left the cluster-in-path portals (code/edges/infrastructure) and the\n  ctx-tenant portals (kuery/quickstart) on their own model — migrating them\n  would change auth behavior; documented why.\n- AGENTS.md §5.7 documents both kits, the sync/verify flow, the two auth models,\n  and a \"use from portalkit, don''t reinvent\" table.\n\nVerified: agents typecheck + build + playwright 13/13; app-studio build clean;\nverify-portalkit green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3421aeadb16e69e8ccb9709a42f9c2a2d255b20c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/3421aeadb16e69e8ccb9709a42f9c2a2d255b20c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDE5NTU1ZjJiZmJhN2I2YTc3NTY4ZmVhNWJkZmZlNzUxMDFkZDJiYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d","sha":"48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d"}],"sha":"19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/19555f2bfba7b6a77568fea5bdffe75101dd2bab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T09:13:57Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T09:13:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(portal): \"Precision Flat\" retheme (light-first, shared UI recipes) (#450)\n\nMove the portal from the dark-default violet glassmorphism look to a flat,\nprecise, light-first language while keeping kedge''s violet identity.\n\n- Light-first: light values are now the @theme base; dark is a flat-ink\n  html.dark override. Default flips to light with a hard fallback in\n  index.html + theme.ts.\n- Fonts: self-host Instrument Sans (UI), Archivo at font-stretch:125% for\n  display/KPI/wordmark, IBM Plex Mono for data (@fontsource). Providers\n  inherit them (dropped root font-family overrides that blocked it).\n- Effects: remove glass, border-beam, card-glow, tilt-card, glow-ring,\n  text-gradient, dot/cross-grid, noise, ambient orbs; restyle island,\n  energy-line, live-dot flat; add the .contour-grid signature background.\n- Shared recipes: new portal/src/assets/kedge-ui.css (.k-card/.k-table/\n  .k-badge/.k-btn/.k-input/.k-eyebrow/.k-kpi) served by the host and reused\n  across every provider via the light DOM — the cross-provider unification\n  layer. ResourceTable + StatusBadge (host + app-studio) adopt it.\n- Terminal stays an intentional dark console on the light page.\n- Radii sweep (16px->12px) and IBM Plex Mono mono-stacks across all 8\n  providers.\n\nHost portal and all 8 provider portals build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f157ee63ae642f5388652d3b439f43b12835104b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/f157ee63ae642f5388652d3b439f43b12835104b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDQ4ZDdhYTExMzQxZTYyZTQ1MjU1NjQ0NjNhYWNhMThhYmY4MzkyNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b","sha":"2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b"}],"sha":"48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/48d7aa11341e62e4525564463aaca18abf83926d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T05:59:19Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T05:59:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: speed up provider image builds (native arm64 + build cache) (#440)\n\nProvider release builds were slow because the multi-arch image was built\nin a single job on an amd64 runner, so the linux/arm64 half ran under QEMU\nemulation — the emulated portal `npm install` and `go build` dominated the\nwall clock.\n\nChanges:\n- provider-release.yaml: split the build across native runners (amd64 on\n  ubuntu-latest, arm64 on ubuntu-24.04-arm, free for this public repo),\n  push each arch by digest, and assemble the multi-arch manifest in a\n  merge job. No more QEMU for the arm64 build. dev-agent stays a simple\n  QEMU multi-arch build (tiny stdlib binary, emulation is cheap there).\n- Add GHA layer cache (type=gha, scoped per provider+arch) to every\n  build-push-action step in provider-release.yaml and images.yaml.\n- All provider Dockerfiles + hub/agent/dev-agent: npm install -> npm ci\n  (lockfiles present) and add BuildKit cache mounts for the npm cache,\n  the Go module cache, and the Go build cache. Add the\n  `# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1` directive to hub/agent/dev-agent so the\n  cache mounts work across BuildKit versions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fdd4503e4ebc624c7e8b78b784f743709741e4b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/fdd4503e4ebc624c7e8b78b784f743709741e4b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDJjYjY5M2MzY2RiMmZmZTU4ZmUxY2QzZmVmY2RjMTg2YTMxZjRiNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e","sha":"941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e"}],"sha":"2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/2cb693c3cdb2ffe58fe1cd3fefcdc186a31f4b4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T16:29:55Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T16:29:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kuery): stop a recursive output schema from EOF-ing the whole MCP endpoint (#372)\n\nThe kuery provider''s /mcp handler panicked on every request: kuery_query was\nregistered with a typed Out (queryOutput -> v1alpha1.QueryStatus -> []ObjectResult),\nand ObjectResult is self-recursive (Relations is map[string][]ObjectResult). The\ngo-sdk schema reflector panics with \"cycle detected\" on recursive types, and\nbecause the server is built per request the panic propagated out of ServeHTTP —\nthe aggregator''s tools/list saw an EOF and dropped kuery entirely (no kuery_query\nAND no kuery_impact federated).\n\nTwo layers of fix so a misbehaving tool can''t take down the provider''s MCP:\n- Register kuery_query with Out=any so the SDK omits output-schema inference (the\n  documented escape hatch) while still populating structured output + JSON content.\n- Wrap each tool registration in safeRegister(): a panic in one AddTool is now\n  recovered and logged, so one bad tool degrades to \"that tool is missing\" instead\n  of crashing the per-request server and EOF-ing the caller.\n\nAdds a regression test driving the real streamable-HTTP handler the way the\naggregator does (initialize + tools/list) and asserting both tools list.\n\nAlso includes in-progress app-studio assistant (eino / approved-plan) changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1fe5ec44aec4f61ac6823405f044449a9c741cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/1fe5ec44aec4f61ac6823405f044449a9c741cf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKDk0MWQ1ZWVjMmY3ZDg3MzQ5N2ZjNzdjOTk5MWI0YjhlMTU3OWQ5M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3","sha":"efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3"}],"sha":"941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/941d5eec2f7d873497fc77c9991b4b8e1579d93e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T14:37:11Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T14:37:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kuery): postgres store fixes + run dev on postgres (#333)\n\n* fix(kuery): bump engine for postgres store fixes + run dev on postgres\n\nRevendor github.com/faroshq/kuery to pick up two Postgres-only query\nfixes (the local store now runs Postgres, so these surfaced):\n\n- owner/linked relation traversal tolerated a JSON scalar owner_refs\n  (\"null\") that aborted with \"cannot extract elements from a scalar\".\n- the ID filter cast id to text so synthetic relation-node ids\n  (\"<uid>:references:0\") no longer abort with \"invalid input syntax for\n  type uuid\".\n\nLocal dev now runs the kuery store on Postgres, matching production —\nSQLite silently masked both bugs. Mirrors the existing app-studio-db\npattern:\n\n- Makefile: kuery-db-up / kuery-db-down spin a throwaway postgres:16\n  container on 127.0.0.1:55433; run-provider-kuery depends on it and\n  always sets KUERY_STORE_DRIVER=postgres (override the DSN via\n  KUERY_STORE_DSN to point at an external Postgres). No SQLite option.\n- Tiltfile + Tiltfile.cluster: kuery-db resource (+ kuery-db-down\n  teardown) under providers-kuery; the kuery resource depends on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* add current release printer\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"245b08dac98114adea5b4cc2780b78a0facdd784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/245b08dac98114adea5b4cc2780b78a0facdd784"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3","node_id":"C_kwDOS5hLPdoAKGVmYzZkNDMyOGU2Zjg0ZGQ1ZjYxMzQzZWMzM2M1MWM4YmQzNWY0ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-kuery/commit/49e660241cc6327d318f37f735c576405a1e6dcd","sha":"49e660241cc6327d318f37f735c576405a1e6dcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/49e660241cc6327d318f37f735c576405a1e6dcd"}],"sha":"efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/efc6d4328e6f84dd5f61343ec33c51c8bd35f4e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/commits/49e660241cc6327d318f37f735c576405a1e6dcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T19:31:12Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T19:31:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(infrastructure): CRD-driven operator (kro helm lifecycle + serve) (#331)\n\n* feat(infrastructure): CRD-driven operator (kro helm lifecycle + serve)\n\nAdd an InfrastructureProvider operator: one CR declares the kro + provider\nimage versions and two kubeconfig Secret refs; the operator continuously\nbootstraps the provider kcp workspace, lifecycles the kro Helm release via the\nhelm CLI (multicluster fork chart + image, kcp-apiexport mode, kind hostAliases\n+ self-cluster patches behind env flags), seeds kro''s kcp-kubeconfig, and owns\nthe provider serve Deployment.\n\n- apis/v1alpha1: InfrastructureProvider CRD (+ generated deepcopy/CRD YAML)\n- operator/: controller-runtime reconciler, helm exec, serve Deployment,\n  bootstrap (shared with the env-driven operator subcommand), kind dev patches\n- main.go: `operator` (env-driven) + `controller` (CRD) subcommands;\n  serveWithConfig extracted; loadControllerConfig honors INFRASTRUCTURE_WORKSPACE_PATH\n- install/operatorseed.go: seed kro from a provided kubeconfig (no SA mint)\n- deploy/chart: operator Deployment + RBAC + CRD + Secrets + CR (operator.enabled),\n  legacy serve/Service gated off in operator mode\n- Dockerfile: bundle the helm CLI for the operator pod\n- Makefile + Tiltfile.cluster: operator dev flow (controller host binary;\n  replaces kro-mgmt-up + infrastructure-init), --validate=false on register\n- README: operator deploy section\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(kuery): bump provider to 788efce\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"96f3eae6ff69b6aab849028c535858011f327f19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/trees/96f3eae6ff69b6aab849028c535858011f327f19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-kuery/git/commits/49e660241cc6327d318f37f735c576405a1e6dcd","verification":{"payload":null,"reaso