 tokens.css name families it\nactually defines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f105a6caa49351e1ce321e3e7fce682f2344494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/trees/9f105a6caa49351e1ce321e3e7fce682f2344494"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/commits/cecd5f95412bd6ee247c522c7669bb1efab1b47c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91695523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valeratrades","id":91695523,"login":"valeratrades","node_id":"U_kgDOBXcpow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/cecd5f95412bd6ee247c522c7669bb1efab1b47c","node_id":"C_kwDOS860CtoAKGNlY2Q1Zjk1NDEyYmQ2ZWUyNDdjNTIyYzc2NjliYjFlZmFiMWI0N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de","sha":"c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de"}],"sha":"cecd5f95412bd6ee247c522c7669bb1efab1b47c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/cecd5f95412bd6ee247c522c7669bb1efab1b47c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91695523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valeratrades","id":91695523,"login":"valeratrades","node_id":"U_kgDOBXcpow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:05:11Z","email":"valeratrades@gmail.com","name":"Valera"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:05:11Z","email":"valeratrades@gmail.com","name":"Valera"},"message":"fix(dashboard): re-home the brand webfonts the uikit stopped shipping\n\nCollateral of the ev_lib 0.9 → 0.13 bump the i18n contract required.\n`uikit::Fonts` left the kit in 0.10.0 (#105, brand assets are not a UI\nkit''s business) and landed nowhere, so the `--font-*` chains in\ntokens.css were naming \"Inter\" and \"Playfair Display\" with nothing\ndefining them — every dashboard surface would have fallen through to\n`ui-sans-serif` / `ui-serif`.\n\nThe four variable TTFs and their OFL licences move here, and\n`src/fonts.rs` injects the same `@font-face` block the kit used to. The\nembed still ships none on purpose: its snapshot is a fallback tile and\nsays so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba26ef278eadc0693e0485eb52f198b268cbfd7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/trees/ba26ef278eadc0693e0485eb52f198b268cbfd7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/commits/c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91695523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valeratrades","id":91695523,"login":"valeratrades","node_id":"U_kgDOBXcpow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de","node_id":"C_kwDOS860CtoAKGM3OWZiNTE2NTgzYjkzNTg1MDI2MDZiN2MzNDM0NGQ3ODdlYTgxZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83","sha":"a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83"}],"sha":"c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/c79fb516583b9358502606b7c34344d787ea81de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91695523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valeratrades","id":91695523,"login":"valeratrades","node_id":"U_kgDOBXcpow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T00:57:01Z","email":"valeratrades@gmail.com","name":"Valera"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T00:58:25Z","email":"valeratrades@gmail.com","name":"Valera"},"message":"feat(i18n)!: migrate onto ev_lib 0.13''s inline-English contract\n\nEvery `tr.t(key)` becomes `t!(tr, key, \"English\")` — 84 sites across the\ndashboard and the embed. `messages/en/common.json` stops being authored\nand starts being generated: `t!` registers its pair with the linker, so a\nsite that *compiles* is in the catalogue whether or not it ever renders,\nwhich is the failure class an SSR-pass extractor drops silently. Both\nsurfaces get the `evinvest-i18n-check` pair — `examples/dump_messages.rs`\nwrites the file, `tests/catalogue.rs` refuses to let it drift from the\ncode, and audits ru/vi/fr/de for stale translations. No English value\nmoved; the only change to either catalogue is key order.\n\nA key can no longer be assembled at runtime, so `core::i18n::status_key`\nbecomes `dashboard::i18n::status_label`, which returns the rendered label:\nthe key and the English it renders are one unit, and a `&''static str` key\npassed around leaves the English stranded where no compiler sees it. It\nleaves `core` for a second reason — both surfaces link `core`, so a `t!`\nsite there would land in both catalogues.\n\n**The embed reads the host''s `<html lang>`, not the `ev_locale` cookie.**\nA first-time reader arriving on `/ru` from a search result has no cookie,\nso the cookie path renders an English widget inside a Russian page. `lang`\nis what the page actually *is*, it is set by every host that serves more\nthan one language, and it is readable the instant the node is attached —\nunlike an attribute, which `RemoteElement` sets in a later effect than the\none that appends the node. `mfe!`''s new `messages:` arm owns that wiring.\n\n**`portfolio.html` becomes `portfolio.{en,ru,vi,fr,de}.html`.** The\nsnapshot is the `RemoteElement` fallback and shows *permanently* if the\nbundle never upgrades, so one `lang=\"en\"` file was not a flash of English\non /ru — it was English forever for anyone with JS off.\n\n`ev_lib::uikit::Fonts` left the kit in 0.10.0 (#105, \"Logo, Fonts and the\nfooter''s baked EV copy leave the kit\"), so the dashboard drops it and\nfalls to the generic tail already written into the `--font-*` chains.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6d37803cf62086664fcc7e0938964322fe54c09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/trees/d6d37803cf62086664fcc7e0938964322fe54c09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/commits/a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91695523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valeratrades","id":91695523,"login":"valeratrades","node_id":"U_kgDOBXcpow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeratrades","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83","node_id":"C_kwDOS860CtoAKGE4MzljOGQzNWE1YzQ1MzE3NWZhNmQwNDViYzk5MTE3ZDFkMzJlODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e","sha":"04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e"}],"sha":"a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/a839c8d35a5c453175fa6d045bc99117d1d32e83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141515065?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/f33na","id":141515065,"login":"f33na","node_id":"U_kgDOCG9ZOQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:54:22Z","email":"141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:54:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(i18n): import JsCast so the wasm client builds again (#38)\n\n`detect()` calls `dyn_into` on a `web_sys::Document` — a `JsCast` method whose\ntrait was never in scope — so the wasm client target has not compiled since #34.\nThe import sits inside the function because `wasm_bindgen` is a wasm-only\ndependency and a module-scope `use` would break the server build.\n\nNothing could have caught it: native checks build the host target, `detect()` is\n`#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]`, and the release container is the first thing\nthat compiles for wasm32. main had taken #34 through #37 with no release tag\nsince v0.1.14, so v0.1.15 was the first build to try — and it failed.","tree":{"sha":"f18795265d1ed87fc294a0ba29a257939a457a25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/trees/f18795265d1ed87fc294a0ba29a257939a457a25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/commits/04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e","verification":{"payload":"tree f18795265d1ed87fc294a0ba29a257939a457a25\nparent e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359\nauthor 33 <141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com> 1787090062 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787090062 +0700\n\nfix(i18n): import JsCast so the wasm client builds again (#38)\n\n`detect()` calls `dyn_into` on a `web_sys::Document` — a `JsCast` method whose\ntrait was never in scope — so the wasm client target has not compiled since #34.\nThe import sits inside the function because `wasm_bindgen` is a wasm-only\ndependency and a module-scope `use` would break the server build.\n\nNothing could have caught it: native checks build the host target, `detect()` is\n`#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]`, and the release container is the first thing\nthat compiles for wasm32. main had taken #34 through #37 with no release tag\nsince v0.1.14, so v0.1.15 was the first build to try — and it failed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhNSOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADz0QAIU8diYEH1i6MVvgF2TTvh0G\nQBcXMYY9gtsCtyt9v6LFg5SQyHLQsN3JWuDo/a8dx2EigCkwmg6leFZG0ohaod5S\noPVJR4BDyakCo8Jy/zm4jKcKbLMe1/WXc/wS/2IY5J1LDmxwumOXIhU+ygZVfIwh\nUNsXJScORxX98HKgXGd4VLSX2pNTBmMTjWtM74OfzqRUif8aXJ5a+K+e7TDFjGXn\ns6Xccgw/+1Of4a48ifbdMEQfBnfBbxNsrL6LAIGojHbolvDqhIZWsB75ydnK4AbI\nVzD7Zd0ZN8t1A3rXU5ivFCJGpLQjsJw71pHjWj6t1ikhORDjETttG3YhNFtcrV+R\nW90aKDahczVMMQ4Icq+E8Szn19gKMqM9F/mT1Gv2SNcXiSB6EWdR/wwkrrzMG2cP\n6ex60YaIVxDl02K7hYWqLKtbcE9Mq7lCoPL4ky4qddbCod4419tMxCPbjooQs6MM\n7F2vy4DduDK2ESkbphMuKJCcZmb+eGl4G1/6Cd2/w2c1fRxEzeYD+FkGtsy+DC5y\noC1W6/ZsiteBiaCoINCThkRBuai9OSleanKt5GO7cwrjQ+osWsVSj7rR8fU/7g9r\nsOY6PCrPv0FYVlW3+3KrVygNS5JU/eA9x1tsavRE3ry1aqqINMVr8KYTMiZzs1eY\nljz3Tn5N9o1LneV55OSl\n=4mHQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T21:54:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e","node_id":"C_kwDOS860CtoAKDA0ZTU3Yzc2ZWZlZmMzYWYwNWYwZDk1YzU2MWRmNzI4OGM4M2NjOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359","sha":"e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359"}],"sha":"04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/04e57c76efefc3af05f0d95c561df7288c83cc8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141515065?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/f33na","id":141515065,"login":"f33na","node_id":"U_kgDOCG9ZOQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:08:29Z","email":"141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:08:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(i18n): translate the property dataset per record (#37)\n\nFinishes the i18n stream: #34 did the dashboard chrome, #36 the embed, this the\npart a reader actually reads.\n\nThe seven buildings in `store` still read English. `terms` and\n`additional_reasoning` now resolve per record from `src/translations.json`,\nkeyed by the building''s UUID — which the seed already fixes so it survives\nreseeds. A sidecar rather than the catalogue because `messages/*/common.json` is\nchrome, while a property''s terms are content: edited per building, arriving from\nthe seed rather than from a designer, and as numerous as the portfolio. Same\nroute the conductor''s publication cards took.\n\nProject names and developers stay as written. They are proper nouns, and\ntransliterating them into four alphabets would make the portfolio harder to\nsearch, not easier to read.\n\nEach entry records the English it was translated from, per field, so an edited\nseed withdraws its own stale translations instead of rendering a translation of\na sentence nobody writes any more.\n\nAlso in here: the last hardcoded labels on the dashboard panels and the embed\nview, the apartment status in the details panel (`status_key` existed and the\nheader used it; this panel kept its own English `match`), and two real compile\nerrors in the embed''s `FactorRow` — which a `cargo check` had been hiding,\nbecause that crate is `#![cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]` and so compiles to\nnothing, and passes, on a native target.","tree":{"sha":"79b46a5ab46e03a006e21fd4bc692d7079ef4c50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/trees/79b46a5ab46e03a006e21fd4bc692d7079ef4c50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/commits/e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359","verification":{"payload":"tree 79b46a5ab46e03a006e21fd4bc692d7079ef4c50\nparent 41d3c35d879eb4671fc86752b79a605d1b08d80b\nauthor 33 <141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com> 1787087309 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787087309 +0700\n\nfeat(i18n): translate the property dataset per record (#37)\n\nFinishes the i18n stream: #34 did the dashboard chrome, #36 the embed, this the\npart a reader actually reads.\n\nThe seven buildings in `store` still read English. `terms` and\n`additional_reasoning` now resolve per record from `src/translations.json`,\nkeyed by the building''s UUID — which the seed already fixes so it survives\nreseeds. A sidecar rather than the catalogue because `messages/*/common.json` is\nchrome, while a property''s terms are content: edited per building, arriving from\nthe seed rather than from a designer, and as numerous as the portfolio. Same\nroute the conductor''s publication cards took.\n\nProject names and developers stay as written. They are proper nouns, and\ntransliterating them into four alphabets would make the portfolio harder to\nsearch, not easier to read.\n\nEach entry records the English it was translated from, per field, so an edited\nseed withdraws its own stale translations instead of rendering a translation of\na sentence nobody writes any more.\n\nAlso in here: the last hardcoded labels on the dashboard panels and the embed\nview, the apartment status in the details panel (`status_key` existed and the\nheader used it; this panel kept its own English `match`), and two real compile\nerrors in the embed''s `FactorRow` — which a `cargo check` had been hiding,\nbecause that crate is `#![cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]` and so compiles to\nnothing, and passes, on a native target.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhMnNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwn8QAJ0nxrHfrQ3rKgbKzunhjyor\n5UPzoJVQip+thahEzlvGrplouaokr2JbqyzvMB7d+jZnr49G0RZ82mBvVdH5VA3L\nV+uUk8HXwx84rtxDYTOacgLb7p5D5hpiiCnBiSFlU/Cg2FrfMufAUZMicQbHm1vV\n88srw/mdMOgcNyXsS18QBsgVudvS+hoeaacQSwkvlGgNGNBHxZOMpP2iPPwlk8b7\npH5QsZhlcwbfhehpewz3xBesx05YukN5lZJLIG3zyW1CnMPquplMFlQQTrifm34E\ntRHKSZeKvbapafSnQl1RSsw8R+xbqJF8zFOAS8lx+EKUfpim7TbfvmWUlqZtagoB\n3BuMvZH0zePdpczpHgZ7nkrBI2Dr9rmEhvcLdnBFVjSQgskQAmZDQ1owdCDwzVaf\nzNxMG6F5xIZLZ4yHSrzF7CjKctY/crzMsu/+LndLUo9y2kdmvgoBRjp+jvjEC+OY\nrw1MM5YuX5mpl3BdB+el27rNjWG2A0360YvHwGY+CiUqmHjZom8arOwOW2F28rdy\nQior9UbiaLQ7ddDp1ju5QvBUOLj77MNsW3zkFhirBlKORtEB4jTqb1o9wTi6BRzx\nBArdehCs5hKfiP4TTiigzS1YtFqQsEQpkqRfbZP2LokmOzop6FYs3aAPA4CsoR80\n6u2WApIGYyVzwwTGvlHd\n=+Nc6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T21:08:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359","node_id":"C_kwDOS860CtoAKGUyZTM4NjE1NTI1MWViOTY3ZDcyMGIyNjc3ZmFlMjIwNGUyNjgzNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commit/41d3c35d879eb4671fc86752b79a605d1b08d80b","sha":"41d3c35d879eb4671fc86752b79a605d1b08d80b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/41d3c35d879eb4671fc86752b79a605d1b08d80b"}],"sha":"e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/e2e386155251eb967d720b2677fae2204e268359"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141515065?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/f33na","id":141515065,"login":"f33na","node_id":"U_kgDOCG9ZOQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/41d3c35d879eb4671fc86752b79a605d1b08d80b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T12:36:41Z","email":"141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T12:36:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(i18n): translate the portfolio embed, and share the harness via core (#36)\n\nThe embed bundle is the widget on the marketing homepage''s Portfolio section —\nthe last EV surface still rendering only English.\n\n# No conductor change was needed\n\nThe bundle is a cross-origin script, but it executes in the *host page''s*\ndocument, so `document.cookie` is the conductor''s. It reads the same `ev_locale`\nthe shell already writes — no attribute plumbing, no second negotiation that\ncould disagree with the header rendered directly above the widget.\n\n# Loading and policy moved to core; the catalogues did not\n\n`core::i18n::Catalogues` holds the parse + `resolve` + `audit`, and each surface\nhands it its own `include_str!`ed files. The dashboard''s copy is operational\n(panel titles, portfolio states) and the embed''s is marketing — one vocabulary\ncannot serve both audiences, so sharing a catalogue would be wrong. Sharing the\n*mechanism* costs nothing and keeps one definition of what \"translated\" means.\n\n`status_key` moved there too, since it maps a `core::domain` type.\n\n`core` keeps its no-dioxus rule: the hook wiring stays per-surface, which is\nwhere it belongs anyway — the two surfaces mount differently.\n\n# Only the labels are translated\n\nThe property descriptions and the market-thesis prose in `view` stay as written.\nThey are authored copy, the same class as the dashboard''s `store` dataset and\nthe same call the public site made for its long-form sections. A translated\nframe around English prose is the worse of the two failures.\n\n# The snapshot stays English, deliberately\n\n`portfolio.html` renders natively at build time, with no document to read a\ncookie from. That is the right answer rather than a gap: the snapshot is what\nthe host shows *until the live bundle upgrades it*, so the canonical locale is\nthe honest thing to bake into a file that has to serve every reader at once.\n\n# Tests that actually run\n\n`src/lib.rs` is `#![cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]`, so anything behind\n`#[cfg(test)]` in that crate never compiles on the host and never runs in CI.\nThe embed''s gates live in `tests/i18n.rs` and pull the module in by path — the\nsame trick `examples/portfolio_snapshot.rs` already uses for `view`.\n\nVerified: 13 tests pass across the workspace, the wasm target compiles, and the\nrendered snapshot is byte-identical to the old hard-coded markup —\n`Premium Asset <span class=\"font-serif italic …\">Portfolio</span>`.","tree":{"sha":"f1050732f12af9e174b76125667c5f53da92306b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/trees/f1050732f12af9e174b76125667c5f53da92306b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/commits/41d3c35d879eb4671fc86752b79a605d1b08d80b","verification":{"payload":"tree f1050732f12af9e174b76125667c5f53da92306b\nparent 3379af5a203d3e9654eeddbdc6a085ab61ffdd50\nauthor 33 <141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com> 1786970201 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786970201 +0700\n\nfeat(i18n): translate the portfolio embed, and share the harness via core (#36)\n\nThe embed bundle is the widget on the marketing homepage''s Portfolio section —\nthe last EV surface still rendering only English.\n\n# No conductor change was needed\n\nThe bundle is a cross-origin script, but it executes in the *host page''s*\ndocument, so `document.cookie` is the conductor''s. It reads the same `ev_locale`\nthe shell already writes — no attribute plumbing, no second negotiation that\ncould disagree with the header rendered directly above the widget.\n\n# Loading and policy moved to core; the catalogues did not\n\n`core::i18n::Catalogues` holds the parse + `resolve` + `audit`, and each surface\nhands it its own `include_str!`ed files. The dashboard''s copy is operational\n(panel titles, portfolio states) and the embed''s is marketing — one vocabulary\ncannot serve both audiences, so sharing a catalogue would be wrong. Sharing the\n*mechanism* costs nothing and keeps one definition of what \"translated\" means.\n\n`status_key` moved there too, since it maps a `core::domain` type.\n\n`core` keeps its no-dioxus rule: the hook wiring stays per-surface, which is\nwhere it belongs anyway — the two surfaces mount differently.\n\n# Only the labels are translated\n\nThe property descriptions and the market-thesis prose in `view` stay as written.\nThey are authored copy, the same class as the dashboard''s `store` dataset and\nthe same call the public site made for its long-form sections. A translated\nframe around English prose is the worse of the two failures.\n\n# The snapshot stays English, deliberately\n\n`portfolio.html` renders natively at build time, with no document to read a\ncookie from. That is the right answer rather than a gap: the snapshot is what\nthe host shows *until the live bundle upgrades it*, so the canonical locale is\nthe honest thing to bake into a file that has to serve every reader at once.\n\n# Tests that actually run\n\n`src/lib.rs` is `#![cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]`, so anything behind\n`#[cfg(test)]` in that crate never compiles on the host and never runs in CI.\nThe embed''s gates live in `tests/i18n.rs` and pull the module in by path — the\nsame trick `examples/portfolio_snapshot.rs` already uses for `view`.\n\nVerified: 13 tests pass across the workspace, the wasm target compiles, and the\nrendered snapshot is byte-identical to the old hard-coded markup —\n`Premium Asset <span class=\"font-serif italic …\">Portfolio</span>`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgwBZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWqIQAEymKMbe19pv3F4T04dkop3p\n2YKpOnC76on118FynAx4S9jjG4wSjZPM7xt6YfDcpruiqZ7ejujTh1V88NIZxNV/\nIcxY4eoLRKqYZRgU6SWBXiLyrQDHjFKgfKLeVAbdcf