60d7c0bbd","sha":"50dd01d6f4e2365876fa8b4739245e560d7c0bbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/50dd01d6f4e2365876fa8b4739245e560d7c0bbd"}],"sha":"3379af5a203d3e9654eeddbdc6a085ab61ffdd50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/3379af5a203d3e9654eeddbdc6a085ab61ffdd50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141515065?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/f33na","id":141515065,"login":"f33na","node_id":"U_kgDOCG9ZOQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/f33na","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/commits/50dd01d6f4e2365876fa8b4739245e560d7c0bbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:20:08Z","email":"141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:20:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(i18n): translate the dashboard chrome into all five locales (#34)\n\nREA was the last EV surface with no internationalisation at all. It is a Dioxus\napp, so it cannot import an npm package — hence `ev_lib`''s `i18n` feature\n(EV-invest/lib#103), which this is the first consumer of.\n\n`messages/<locale>/common.json` here is byte-for-byte the shape the public site\nuses: `en/common.json` is flat `key -> text`, every other locale is\n`key -> {en, t}` carrying the English it was translated from. That is what lets\n`ev_lib::i18n::policy` apply the same rules `npm run i18n:check` applies there,\nand it means a catalogue moves between the two without conversion.\n\nBaked in with `include_str!` rather than fetched: this is a wasm SPA, so a\nruntime fetch means the first paint renders untranslated and then reflows, and a\nfailed fetch means no copy at all.\n\nA zone never negotiates for itself. The shell has already read Accept-Language\nand written the `ev_locale` cookie; guessing again in the zone could disagree\nwith the header rendered directly above the view. So `detect()` reads the cookie\nand nothing else — no `navigator.language` fallback.\n\nProject names, developers, terms, reasoning in `store.rs` are content authored\nper building, not chrome. Same call publications took: it stays in the language\nit was written in until there is a per-record translation to serve.\n\n`header.rs` and `details.rs` each carried their own `ApartmentStatus -> &str`\nmapping — already the drift a shared key set exists to prevent. Both now go\nthrough `i18n::status_key`, so a building cannot be \"Purchased\" in one panel and\nsomething else in another.\n\n`header.buildings` is a plain label, not a plural: it is the breadcrumb root,\nand the dashboard renders no building count today. Inventing a plural for a\nstring nothing renders would be worse than not having one.\n\nVerified: 9 tests pass (4 new, including the drift audit — the in-repo mirror of\nthe site''s i18n:check), clippy clean for the files touched, rustfmt clean.\n\nBLOCKED: needs `ev_lib` 0.8.0 on crates.io. The workspace dep is bumped to\n^0.8.0 and Cargo.lock is deliberately left alone — it cannot resolve until the\npublish lands, at which point cargo updates it on the first build. Verified\nlocally against the 0.8.0 source through the `[patch.crates-io]` hook the\nworkspace already keeps commented out for exactly this.","tree":{"sha":"06a2123b497ad417763058cd04df1a529a12e3dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/trees/06a2123b497ad417763058cd04df1a529a12e3dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EV-invest/real_estate_allocation/git/commits/50dd01d6f4e2365876fa8b4739245e560d7c0bbd","verification":{"payload":"tree 06a2123b497ad417763058cd04df1a529a12e3dc\nparent e3083b3ae1c201ac371e431b0e75b5ea379128f5\nauthor 33 <141515065+f33na@users.noreply.github.com> 1786749608 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786749608 +0700\n\nfeat(i18n): translate the dashboard chrome into all five locales (#34)\n\nREA was the last EV surface with no internationalisation at all. It is a Dioxus\napp, so it cannot import an npm package — hence `ev_lib`''s `i18n` feature\n(EV-invest/lib#103), which this is the first consumer of.\n\n`messages/<locale>/common.json` here is byte-for-byte the shape the public site\nuses: `en/common.json` is flat `key -> text`, every other locale is\n`key -> {en, t}` carrying the English it was translated from. That is what lets\n`ev_lib::i18n::policy` apply the same rules `npm run i18n:check` applies there,\nand it means a catalogue moves between the two without conversion.\n\nBaked in with `include_str!` rather than fetched: this is a wasm SPA, so a\nruntime fetch means the first paint renders untranslated and then reflows, and a\nfailed fetch means no copy at all.\n\nA zone never negotiates for itself. The shell has already read Accept-Language\nand written the `ev_locale` cookie; guessing again in the zone could disagree\nwith the header rendered directly above the view. So `detect()` reads the cookie\nand nothing else — no `navigator.language` fallback.\n\nProject names, developers, terms, reasoning in `store.rs` are content authored\nper building, not chrome. Same call publications took: it stays in the language\nit was written in until there is a per-record translation to serve.\n\n`header.rs` and `details.rs` each carried their own `ApartmentStatus -> &str`\nmapping — already the drift a shared key set exists to prevent. Both now go\nthrough `i18n::status_key`, so a building cannot be \"Purchased\" in one panel and\nsomething else in another.\n\n`header.buildings` is a plain label, not a plural: it is the breadcrumb root,\nand the dashboard renders no building count today. Inventing a plural for a\nstring nothing renders would be worse than not having one.\n\nVerified: 9 tests pass (4 new, including the drift audit — the in-repo mirror of\nthe site''s i18n:check), clippy clean for the files touched, rustfmt clean.\n\nBLOCKED: needs `ev_lib` 0.8.0 on crates.io. The workspace dep is bumped to\n^0.8.0 and Cargo.lock is deliberately left alone — it cannot resolve until the\npublish lands, at which point cargo updates it on the first build. Verified\nlocally against the 0.8.0 source through the `[patch.crates-io]` hook the\nworkspace already keeps commented out for exactly this.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqf6KoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxowQAHZrGywyrpcPU9q8nwuc+md/\nQsTFCvogIGqbUJex4gUinB+KWbofqaDRN2mJJhfXecfJ/Q56cgZhvuv9cqky8b/3\nXMioz/gaL4AKxjEmbxPr7x2Iexn8DEKSkSQwgMGNlljzfgDqrZ0IGEyTiTPULw7n\nTu2KnUDGpm4klGObMWRFj4hTlOUG2Fv9P0mVzev8ZXnH4P3OXYbbYSmObuO9EnX5\ndfojU/sLSFlweUiAHs67p4UpgXCFUki4hqmbedhThLamnWLt6si9djvLQSeCjVMB\nGw+VWNYCQPSKKRbkybWQD9HODMb2D6wg77a9ItxnoSICS33KNXCISObSYN/wT801\nzmZLxIb0/cCMasZ+l5s4983CP5g15oEnfGb8KkOJd7Yzi4aZPFecDNfT+qTdP6Ax\noV/ihsLStD7zfeanvfE/ZoYjbeqYssd/6kP2dZ2Iq8vnEtZ0A73nOlVI5ZzGpSdw\n51k8ykZkdecnkkuMKM7rf5kIJ2p1LkLNXBnOVp6osFB2FBlKBEA7AmSBoH+9DVcH\nOyGcv8ofmA5xZI5/ja/djQPyvg21aOgekfC6R/9zWp9pTBTv683eSDzAD+rtgES+\nlcfgPQMUzOTLbWlkT0MwVoheBDGUgwua6/1SG28RknqTfjxnmqp9NUIgFLpf2t8O\nykluyE4qaLTgpAbXPvZb\n=IcMY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T23:20:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"