ubscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/3a45fe90b8d44f92fa7cbbc45b57a3d855439b5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:26:38Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:26:38Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"test(scheduler): verify the push path against a real remote\n\nThe push path was only ever exercised on a remote-less local repo (where it is\ncorrectly skipped). Add integration tests against a local bare repo standing in\nfor origin (no network) covering both real-remote behaviours:\n\n- land_pushes_to_a_configured_remote: landing pushes base and the merged commit\n  actually arrives on origin (asserted via ls-remote from the work repo).\n- land_errors_when_a_configured_push_fails: a configured origin whose push fails\n  surfaces an error and is NOT silently skipped (only a *missing* remote skips).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8b98ec385fa6fccbda28734deecd8a53b624e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/trees/f8b98ec385fa6fccbda28734deecd8a53b624e89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/commits/3a45fe90b8d44f92fa7cbbc45b57a3d855439b5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/3a45fe90b8d44f92fa7cbbc45b57a3d855439b5f","node_id":"C_kwDOS8_zPtoAKDNhNDVmZTkwYjhkNDRmOTJmYTdjYmJjNDViNTdhM2Q4NTU0MzliNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6","sha":"f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6"}],"sha":"3a45fe90b8d44f92fa7cbbc45b57a3d855439b5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/3a45fe90b8d44f92fa7cbbc45b57a3d855439b5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:24:21Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:24:21Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"feat(scheduler): resolve merge mode per-workflow (workspace.merge)\n\nIssue 03 follow-up: merge mode was global-only, so a repo wanting strict linear\nhistory (fast-forward) couldn''t coexist with a concurrent workflow needing merge\ncommits for diverged parallel branches.\n\nMirror workspace.gate end to end:\n- store: Workspace.merge: Option<MergeMode> (new storable enum, kebab-case wire\n  form), persisted as an Option<String> column so pre-column rows read as None.\n- api: WorkspaceBody.merge on POST /workflows, threaded into the Workspace.\n- engine: EffectiveGit.merge resolved workspace ?? global; merge::land reads\n  eff.merge instead of cfg.merge. A standalone task uses the global merge.\n\nTests: store roundtrip, effective resolution (workspace wins / None inherits /\nstandalone), and a land() test proving an effective ''merge'' integrates a diverged\nbranch even when the global config is ''fast-forward''.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be00694a8ea3c740ebd32499b6d8cc78466d648b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/trees/be00694a8ea3c740ebd32499b6d8cc78466d648b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/commits/f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6","node_id":"C_kwDOS8_zPtoAKGY5YWQwOWYwZjU4ODM4NDFhOWMxMTBjNmNhMDFmMjVmZDUwNjJhZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58","sha":"08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58"}],"sha":"f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/f9ad09f0f5883841a9c110c6ca01f25fd5062ad6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:18:31Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:18:31Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"feat(scheduler): bootstrap a scoped Claude allow-list into new worktrees\n\nHeadless Claude Code agents stall on per-tool approval prompts in a\nnever-trusted worktree (docs/issues/01). The committed default\n`permission_flags: claude: []` relied on each target repo committing a\n`.claude/settings.json` allow-list by hand.\n\nprovision() now writes a repo-scoped `.claude/settings.json` allow-list into\neach new worktree when the tool is `claude` and the target repo does not already\ncommit one. This keeps the grant repo-scoped: it never touches the global\n`~/.claude.json` bypass-mode flag, and a repo that owns its posture is never\noverwritten. Best-effort and idempotent across reclaims.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c5ff91d73551dddc538ca360adf970ddee46443d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/trees/c5ff91d73551dddc538ca360adf970ddee46443d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/commits/08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58","node_id":"C_kwDOS8_zPtoAKDA4ZTA3MDEzYzFiZmY5YWQ2NDZlOWVkZTRkMDU1YTE0YTc3MzJjNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4","sha":"4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4"}],"sha":"08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/08e07013c1bff9ad646e9ede4d055a14a7732c58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:17:08Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:17:08Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"chore: ignore local bin/ (per-machine hcom binary dir)\n\nThe hcom CLI installs into ./bin, which is machine-local and should not be\ntracked. Ignore it like the other runtime/secret dirs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78283646140f5fa9ac077c1a3cfbd3c0b2b20e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/trees/78283646140f5fa9ac077c1a3cfbd3c0b2b20e06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/commits/4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4","node_id":"C_kwDOS8_zPtoAKDQ5MjFkZDliYjQ2ZWRlOWJhOTFhYTU2NzE3ZTMzMjY1OTk5OWNmZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lazybones/commit/76902896f7bb799b80bab719251e5838270f61fa","sha":"76902896f7bb799b80bab719251e5838270f61fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/76902896f7bb799b80bab719251e5838270f61fa"}],"sha":"4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/4921dd9bb46ede9ba91aa56717e332659999cfe4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/commits/76902896f7bb799b80bab719251e5838270f61fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T06:13:01Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T06:13:01Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"feat(engine): make agent workflows production-viable on any repo/stack\n\nThree blockers surfaced running a real 4-task workflow (BE/FE + tests) on a\nnon-Rust, remote-less target repo with headless Claude Code agents. All fixed;\nthe workflow then landed 4/4 green.\n\n- Per-workflow gate (workspace.gate): tasks no longer forced through the global\n  cargo gate; a Node/Python/Go repo sets its own (or [] to disable). Resolves\n  task -> workflow -> global. (docs/issues/02)\n- Headless permission posture configurable per tool (permission_flags); default\n  lazybones.yaml uses a repo-scoped allow-list instead of --dangerously-skip-\n  permissions to avoid a global bypass-mode acceptance. (docs/issues/01)\n- Landing resilience (merge.rs): push() skips a missing remote (land locally)\n  instead of failing; default merge mode -> `merge` so diverging parallel task\n  branches integrate via a merge commit rather than failing --ff-only. (docs/issues/03)\n\nGate green: cargo test --workspace + clippy -D warnings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9be4cab225a3688e68b798f998d439e2f34e9cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/trees/9be4cab225a3688e68b798f998d439e2f34e9cea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lazybones/git/commits/76902896f7bb799b80bab719251e5838270f61fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_